(13993,'Don\'t be afraid; we\'re here to aid you. We\'re grateful for the defense you\'ve granted us within our former home, and as a measure of thanks, we\'ve come to help you return quickly to the Plaguelands should you need it. My compatriot can explain the process further; you\'ll find him where the arcane energies are strongest within this city.','우린 당신을 도우러 왔으니 두려워하지 마십시오. 살아 생전 우리 고향이었던 곳을 지켜주어 정말 고맙게 생각합니다. 그 보답으로 당신이 역병지대로 최대한 빨리 돌아갈 수 있도록 돕겠습니다. 제 동료가 앞으로의 일정에 대해 설명해 드릴 겁니다. 이 도시에서 마력이 가장 충만한 곳으로 가면 그를 만나게 될 겁니다.','N’ayez pas peur, nous sommes là pour vous aider. Nous vous sommes reconnaissants de l’aide que vous avez apportée à notre ancien foyer. Pour vous remercier, nous sommes venus vous aider à gagner rapidement les Maleterres, au cas où ce serait nécessaire. Mon compatriote vous expliquera le processus mieux que moi. Vous le trouverez en ville, là où les énergies arcaniques sont les plus puissantes.','Keine Angst; wir sind hier, um Euch zu helfen. Wir fühlen uns für Eure Verteidigung in unserer ehemaligen Heimat zu Dank verpflichtet, deshalb wollen wir Euch als Zeichen unserer Anerkennung helfen, bei Bedarf rasch in die Pestländer zurückzukehren. Mein Landsmann kann Euch alles Weitere erklären; Ihr findet ihn dort, wo die arkanen Energien dieser Stadt am stärksten sind.','别害怕；我们是来帮你的。在我们的家园保卫战中，你曾经慷慨地伸出援手；你想要迅速返回东瘟疫之地是吧，这点我们可以做到的。我的同伴会向你解释要怎么做；去城内的魔法区域找他吧。','別怕;我們是來幫你的。我們很感謝你在我們先前的家園給予的保護，做為感謝的方式，如果你需要，我們可以讓你快速回到瘟疫之地。我的同伴會解釋進一步的程序;你可以在城市中秘法能量最強的地方找到他。','No tengas miedo. Estamos aquí para ayudarte. Te agradecemos tus esfuerzos por defendernos en nuestro antiguo hogar, y como agradecimiento hemos venido a ayudarte a regresar rápidamente a las Tierras de la Peste cuando lo necesites. Mi compatriota te puede explicar más sobre el proceso. Lo encontrarás en esta ciudad, en donde las energías Arcanas tienen su máxima potencia.','No tengas miedo. Estamos aquí para ayudarte. Te agradecemos tus esfuerzos por defendernos en nuestro antiguo hogar, y como agradecimiento hemos venido a ayudarte a regresar rápidamente a las Tierras de la Peste cuando lo necesites. Mi compatriota te puede explicar más sobre el proceso. Lo encontrarás en esta ciudad, en donde las energías Arcanas tienen su máxima potencia.','Не бойся, мы пришли помочь тебе. Мы благодарны за то, что ты защитил наш прежний дом, и поможем тебе быстро вернуться в Чумные земли, если ты того хочешь. Мой соплеменник может рассказать тебе о процессе подробнее – ты найдешь его там, где магическая энергия наиболее сильна в этом городе.','Don\'t be afraid; we\'re here to aid you. We\'re grateful for the defense you\'ve granted us within our former home, and as a measure of thanks, we\'ve come to help you return quickly to the Plaguelands should you need it. My compatriot can explain the process further; you\'ll find him where the arcane energies are strongest within this city.','우린 당신을 도우러 왔으니 두려워하지 마세요. 살아 생전 우리 고향이었던 곳을 지켜주어 정말 고맙게 생각한답니다. 그 보답으로 당신이 역병지대로 최대한 빨리 돌아갈 수 있도록 돕겠습니다. 제 동료가 앞으로의 일정에 대해 설명해 드릴 겁니다. 이 도시에서 마력이 가장 충만한 곳으로 가면 그를 만나게 될 거예요.','N’ayez pas peur, nous sommes là pour vous aider. Nous vous sommes reconnaissants de l’aide que vous avez apportée à notre ancien foyer. Pour vous remercier, nous sommes venus vous aider à gagner rapidement les Maleterres, au cas où ce serait nécessaire. Mon compatriote vous expliquera le processus mieux que moi. Vous le trouverez en ville, là où les énergies arcaniques sont les plus puissantes.','Keine Angst; wir sind hier, um Euch zu helfen. Wir fühlen uns für Eure Verteidigung in unserer ehemaligen Heimat zu Dank verpflichtet, deshalb wollen wir Euch als Zeichen unserer Anerkennung helfen, bei Bedarf rasch in die Pestländer zurückzukehren. Mein Landsmann kann Euch alles Weitere erklären; Ihr findet ihn dort, wo die arkanen Energien dieser Stadt am stärksten sind.','别害怕；我们是来帮你的。在我们的家园保卫战中，你曾经慷慨地伸出援手；你想要迅速返回东瘟疫之地是吧，这点我们可以做到的。我的同伴会向你解释要怎么做；去城内的魔法区域找他吧。','別怕;我們是來幫你的。我們很感謝你在我們先前的家園給予的保護，做為感謝的方式，如果你需要，我們可以讓你快速回到瘟疫之地。我的同伴會解釋進一步的程序;你可以在城市中秘法能量最強的地方找到他。','No tengas miedo. Estamos aquí para ayudarte. Te agradecemos tus esfuerzos por defendernos en nuestro antiguo hogar, y como agradecimiento hemos venido a ayudarte a regresar rápidamente a las Tierras de la Peste cuando lo necesites. Mi compatriota te puede explicar más sobre el proceso. Lo encontrarás en esta ciudad, en donde las energías Arcanas tienen su máxima potencia.','No tengas miedo. Estamos aquí para ayudarte. Te agradecemos tus esfuerzos por defendernos en nuestro antiguo hogar, y como agradecimiento hemos venido a ayudarte a regresar rápidamente a las Tierras de la Peste cuando lo necesites. Mi compatriota te puede explicar más sobre el proceso. Lo encontrarás en esta ciudad, en donde las energías Arcanas tienen su máxima potencia.','Не бойся, мы пришли помочь тебе. Мы благодарны за то, что ты защитил наш прежний дом, и поможем тебе быстро вернуться в Чумные земли, если ты того хочешь. Мой соплеменник может рассказать тебе о процессе подробнее – ты найдешь его там, где магическая энергия наиболее сильна в этом городе.'),
(13994,'I am truly sorry, $c, but as your spirit has never before experienced the horrors that lie in wait within the burning wreck of Stratholme, our magic cannot carry you to the city.','$c|1이여;여;, 정말 죄송하지만 우리 마법으로는 아직 그 도시의 불타는 잔해 속에 도사린 공포를 겪어보지 못한 영혼을 스트라솔름으로 데려다드릴 수 없습니다.','Je regrette, $c, mais votre esprit n\'a jamais eu l\'expérience des horreurs qui vous attendent dans les ruines en flammes de Stratholme. Notre magie ne peut donc pas vous y transporter.','Es tut mir wirklich leid, $C, aber da Euer Geist noch nie das Grauen erlebt hat, das innerhalb der brennenden Trümmer von Stratholme liegt, kann unsere Magie Euch nicht zur Stadt bringen.','抱歉，$C，斯坦索姆燃烧的废墟中弥漫着难以言说的恐怖气氛，而你尚未经历过这一切，我们没法将你传送到斯坦索姆去。','我真的很抱歉，$c，因為你的靈魂從未體驗過斯坦索姆燃燒殘骸裡等待的恐懼，我們的魔法不能將你帶到那個城市。','Realmente lo siento, $c, pero como tu espíritu nunca ha sufrido los horrores que acontecen en Stratholme, nuestra magia no te puede llevar a la ciudad.','Realmente lo siento, $c, pero como tu espíritu nunca ha sufrido los horrores que acontecen en Stratholme, nuestra magia no te puede llevar a la ciudad.','Мне правда жаль, $c, но, поскольку твой дух никогда не испытывал ужасов, что поджидают жертв в пылающих развалинах Стратхольма, наше волшебство не может перенести тебя в город.','I am truly sorry, $c, but as your spirit has never before experienced the horrors that lie in wait within the burning wreck of Stratholme, our magic cannot carry you to the city.','$c|1이여;여;, 정말 죄송하지만 우리 마법으로는 아직 그 도시의 불타는 잔해 속에 도사린 공포를 겪어보지 못한 영혼을 스트라솔름으로 데려다드릴 수 없습니다.','Je regrette, $c, mais votre esprit n\'a jamais eu l\'expérience des horreurs qui vous attendent dans les ruines en flammes de Stratholme. Notre magie ne peut donc pas vous y transporter.','Es tut mir wirklich leid, $C, aber da Euer Geist noch nie das Grauen erlebt hat, das innerhalb der brennenden Trümmer von Stratholme liegt, kann unsere Magie Euch nicht zur Stadt bringen.','抱歉，$C，斯坦索姆燃烧的废墟中弥漫着难以言说的恐怖气氛，而你尚未经历过这一切，我们没法将你传送到斯坦索姆去。','我真的很抱歉，$c，因為你的靈魂從未體驗過斯坦索姆燃燒殘骸裡等待的恐懼，我們的魔法不能將你帶到那個城市。','Realmente lo siento, $c, pero como tu espíritu nunca ha sufrido los horrores que acontecen en Stratholme, nuestra magia no te puede llevar a la ciudad.','Realmente lo siento, $c, pero como tu espíritu nunca ha sufrido los horrores que acontecen en Stratholme, nuestra magia no te puede llevar a la ciudad.','Мне правда жаль, $c, но, поскольку твой дух никогда не испытывал ужасов, что поджидают жертв в пылающих развалинах Стратхольма, наше волшебство не может перенести тебя в город.'),
(13995,'I can see in your eyes you\'re no stranger to the tragedy within Stratholme. If you wish to end the miserable existence of the poor souls trapped therein, step into the circle. It leads directly to the gates of the burning city itself.','당신의 눈을 보니 스트라솔름의 비극을 이미 경험해 보신 것 같군요. 그곳에 비참하게 갇혀 있는 딱한 영혼들을 없앨 작정이라면 원안으로 들어가십시오. 불타는 도시의 문으로 바로 이동하게 될 겁니다.','Je lis dans vos yeux que la tragédie qui se déroule à l’intérieur de Stratholme ne vous est pas inconnue. Si vous souhaitez aider à mettre un terme aux misérables existences des pauvres âmes qui y sont piégées, entrez dans le cercle. Il mène directement aux portes de la ville en flammes.','Ich kann in Euren Augen sehen, dass Euch die Tragödie von Stratholme nicht fremd ist. Solltet Ihr dem elenden Dasein dieser armen Seelen, die darin gefangen sind, ein Ende bereiten wollen, so tretet in den Kreis. Er wird Euch direkt zu den Toren der Stadt bringen.','我从你的眼神儿中看得出来，你对斯坦索姆的悲剧事件并不陌生。如果你想要解救那些被困在斯坦索姆中的可怜亡魂，就站到这法阵中来。它会直接将你传送到那座燃烧的城市入口处的。','從你的眼睛裡我看的出來你對斯坦索姆的災難並不陌生。如果你想結束那些受困的可憐靈魂不幸命運，就踏進圈圈裡。它會直接將你帶到燃燒的城市入口。','En tus ojos veo que no eres ajeno a la tragedia de Stratholme. Si deseas acabar con la miserable existencia de las almas en pena de allí, colócate en medio del círculo. Te llevará directamente a las puedras de la ciudad ardiente.','En tus ojos veo que no eres ajeno a la tragedia de Stratholme. Si deseas acabar con la miserable existencia de las almas en pena de allí, colócate en medio del círculo. Te llevará directamente a las puedras de la ciudad ardiente.','По вашим глазам видно, что трагедия в Стратхольме глубоко тронула вас. Если вы хотите освободить бедные души от их жалкого прозябания там, встаньте в круг. Он ведет прямо ко входу в горящий город.','I can see in your eyes you\'re no stranger to the tragedy within Stratholme. If you wish to end the miserable existence of the poor souls trapped therein, step into the circle. It leads directly to the gates of the burning city itself.','당신의 눈을 보니 스트라솔름의 비극을 이미 경험해 보신 것 같군요. 그곳에 갇혀 비참하게 존재하고 있는 딱한 영혼들을 없앨 작정이라면 원 안으로 들어가세요. 불타는 도시의 문으로 바로 이동하게 될 거예요.','Je lis dans vos yeux que la tragédie qui se déroule à l’intérieur de Stratholme ne vous est pas inconnue. Si vous souhaitez aider à mettre un terme aux misérables existences des pauvres âmes qui y sont piégées, entrez dans le cercle. Il mène directement aux portes de la ville en flammes.','Ich kann in Euren Augen sehen, dass Euch die Tragödie von Stratholme nicht fremd ist. Solltet Ihr dem elenden Dasein dieser armen Seelen, die darin gefangen sind, ein Ende bereiten wollen, so tretet in den Kreis. Er wird Euch direkt zu den Toren der Stadt bringen.','我从你的眼神儿中看得出来，你对斯坦索姆的悲剧事件并不陌生。如果你想要解救那些被困在斯坦索姆中的可怜亡魂，就站到这法阵中来。它会直接将你传送到那座燃烧的城市入口处的。','從你的眼睛裡我看的出來你對斯坦索姆的災難並不陌生。如果你想結束那些受困的可憐靈魂不幸命運，就踏進圈圈裡。它會直接將你帶到燃燒的城市入口。','En tus ojos veo que no eres ajeno a la tragedia de Stratholme. Si deseas acabar con la miserable existencia de las almas en pena de allí, colócate en medio del círculo. Te llevará directamente a las puedras de la ciudad ardiente.','En tus ojos veo que no eres ajeno a la tragedia de Stratholme. Si deseas acabar con la miserable existencia de las almas en pena de allí, colócate en medio del círculo. Te llevará directamente a las puedras de la ciudad ardiente.','По вашим глазам видно, что трагедия в Стратхольме глубоко тронула вас. Если вы хотите освободить бедные души от их жалкого прозябания там, встаньте в круг. Он ведет прямо ко входу в горящий город.'),
(14018,'Be careful out in the desert, $c.','$c|1이여;여;, 사막에서는 몸조심해야 합니다.','Soyez $gprudent:prudente; dans le désert, $c.','Seid draußen in der Wüste vorsichtig, $C.','在沙漠里要多加小心，$c。','在沙漠裡要小心，$c。','Ten cuidado en el desierto, $c.','Ten cuidado en el desierto, $c.','Будь осторожнее в пустыне, $c.','','','','','','','','',''),
(14364,'','','','','','','','','','The spirits of this place are focused against your kind, $r. Perhaps if you win this tower in the flesh, I will be able to aid you.','이곳의 영혼들은 그대의 종족의 싸움에 주의를 기울이고 있습니다, $r|1이여;여;. 아마 그대가 살아서 이 경비탑을 지키는 데 성공한다면, 내 그대를 도울 수 있을 겁니다.','Les esprits de ce lieu détestent les gens de votre sorte, $r. Peut-être que si vous vous emparez personnellement de cette tour, je pourrai vous aider.','Die Geister dieses Orts sind Euch gegenüber feindlich gesinnt, $R. Vielleicht werde ich Euch helfen können, wenn Ihr diesen Turm im richtigen Leben erobert.','似乎此地的鬼魂们并不欢迎你，$r。如果你能攻下这座哨塔，我可以考虑帮助你。','這個地方的靈魂對你的族人很不友善，$r。如果你能贏得這座哨塔，我或許能夠幫你。','Los espíritus de este lugar están en contra de los de tu clase, $r. Quizás si logras conquistar la torre con la espada yo pueda ayudarte.','Los espíritus de este lugar están en contra de los de tu clase, $r. Quizás si logras conquistar la torre con la espada yo pueda ayudarte.','Духи этого места не приемлют таких, как вы, $r. Возможно, если вы завоюете эту башню, я смогу вам помочь.'),
(14385,'Greetings, citizen. I ask that you move along if you have nothing to ask of me.','안녕하신가요, 스톰윈드의 시민이여. 내게 하실 말씀이 없으시면 가던 길을 가 주셨으면 합니다만...','Salutations, $gcitoyen:citoyenne;. Je vous prie de circuler si vous n’avez rien d’autre à me demander.','Seid gegrüßt, Bürger. Bitte geht weiter, wenn ich Euch nicht behilflich sein kann.','朋友，向你致意。如果你没什么要帮忙的就径直往前走吧。','你好，居民。如果你沒什麼事要問我，那就請你走吧。','Saludos, $gciudadano:ciudadana;. Te ruego que sigas tu camino si es que no tienes nada que preguntarme.','Saludos, $gciudadano:ciudadana;. Te ruego que sigas tu camino si es que no tienes nada que preguntarme.','Приветствую вас, горожанин. Проходите, пожалуйста, если не хотите ни о чем меня спрашивать.','','','','','','','','',''),
(14386,'Marshal Windsor has been expecting you, $n. Unfortunately, he is currently indisposed. He should be returning shortly.','윈저 치안대장님께서 당신을 기다리고 계셨습니다, $n. 안타깝게도, 그분께서는 가벼운 병을 앓고 계시지만 곧 자리로 복귀하실 겁니다.','Le maréchal Windsor vous attend, $n. Il est malheureusement indisposé pour le moment, mais il devrait revenir sous peu.','Marschall Windsor hat Euch bereits erwartet, $n. Unglücklicherweise ist er gerade unpässlich. Er sollte jeden Moment wieder da sein.','温德索尔元帅一直都盼着你呢，$n。不幸的是，眼下他身染微恙，不过应该很快就能康复。','溫德索爾元帥一直在等你，$n。不幸的是，他現在不太舒服。不過應該很快就會恢復了。','El mariscal Windsor te ha estado esperando, $n. Desafortunadamente, ahora mismo está indispuesto. Seguro que pronto podrá atenderte.','El mariscal Windsor te ha estado esperando, $n. Desafortunadamente, ahora mismo está indispuesto. Seguro que pronto podrá atenderte.','Маршал Виндзор ожидал вас, $n. К сожалению, его сейчас нет на месте. Должно быть, он скоро вернется.','','','','','','','','',''),
(14387,'You made it! Outstanding! Marshal Windsor has been expecting you. Would you like me to signal him now?','해냈군요! 대단합니다! 윈저 치안대장님께서 당신이 오시기를 고대하셨지요. 지금 그분께 연락을 취해 드릴까요?','Vous avez réussi ! Formidable ! Le maréchal Windsor vous attend. Voulez-vous que je le fasse prévenir tout de suite ?','Ihr habt es geschafft! Außerordentlich! Marschall Windsor hat Euch bereits erwartet. Möchtet Ihr, dass ich ihm jetzt Bescheid sage?','你做到了！太了不起了！温德索尔元帅一直都盼着你呢。你要我现在就通知他吗？','你辦到了!太傑出了!溫德索爾元帥一直在等你。要不要我現在去通知他?','¡Lo has conseguido! ¡Excelente! El mariscal Windsor te ha estado esperando. ¿Deseas que lo llame?','¡Lo has conseguido! ¡Excelente! El mariscal Windsor te ha estado esperando. ¿Deseas que lo llame?','У вас получилось! Потрясающе! Маршал Виндзор как раз ждет вас. Хотите, чтобы я подал ему сигнал?','','','','','','','','',''),
(14388,'Let Marshal Windsor know that I am ready.','치안대장 윈저 님께 준비가 됐다고 전해 주십시오.','Faites savoir au maréchal Windsor que je suis prêt.','Lasst Marschall Windsor wissen, dass ich bereit bin.','请转告温德索尔元帅我已准备就绪。','讓溫德索爾元帥知道我準備好了。','Haz saber al mariscal Windsor que ya estoy listo.','Haz saber al mariscal Windsor que ya estoy listo.','Пусть маршал Виндзор знает, что я готов.','Let Marshal Windsor know that I am ready.','치안대장 윈저 님께 준비가 됐다고 전해 주세요.','Faites savoir au maréchal Windsor que je suis prête.','Lasst Marschall Windsor wissen, dass ich bereit bin.','请转告温德索尔元帅我已准备就绪。','讓溫德索爾元帥知道我準備好了。','Haz saber al mariscal Windsor que ya estoy lista.','Haz saber al mariscal Windsor que ya estoy lista.','Пусть маршал Виндзор знает, что я готова.'),
(14389,'The signal has been sent. He should be arriving shortly.','신호를 보냈으니 윈저 님께서 금방 도착하실 겁니다.','Le signal est parti. Il devrait arriver incessamment.','Man hat Bescheid gegeben. Er sollte in Kürze hier sein.','我已经通知了温德索尔元帅。他应该很快就能赶到这儿。','信號已發出。他應該很快就會到了。','Ya he enviado la señal. Seguro que llegará pronto.','Ya he enviado la señal. Seguro que llegará pronto.','Сигнал отправлен. Он должен скоро появиться.','','','','','','','','',''),
(14390,'Hail, champion. The tale of your deeds will be told throughout the ages. Perhaps one day, a statue of you will stand amongst the heroes of Stormwind.','어서 오십시오, 영웅이여. 당신의 공적에 대한 이야기가 세대에 걸쳐 전해질 것이라 믿습니다. 아마 언젠가, 당신의 동상이 저 스톰윈드의 영웅들 사이에 세워질 날이 있겠군요.','Salut à vous, $gchampion:championne;. Les récits de vos exploits seront contés à travers les âges. Un jour, votre statue prendra peut-être place parmi celles des héros de Hurlevent.','Seid gegrüßt, Held. Man wird noch jahrelang über Eure ruhmreichen Taten sprechen. Vielleicht wird eines Tages auch eine Statue von Euch inmitten der Helden von Sturmwind stehen.','勇士，向你致敬。你所立下的丰功伟绩将代代传颂。或许有一天，你的雕像会矗立在暴风城的英雄谷。','嗨，勇士。你的事蹟將會被世代傳誦。或許有一天，你的雕像會矗立在暴風城的英雄之間。','Saludos, Campeón. Los relatos de tus hazañas se harán eternos. Quizás algún día se erija una estatua en tu honor entre los héroes de Ventormenta.','Saludos, Campeón. Los relatos de tus hazañas se harán eternos. Quizás algún día se erija una estatua en tu honor entre los héroes de Ventormenta.','Славься, защитник! Легенды о ваших деяниях будут жить в веках. Может быть, однажды ваша статуя займет место среди других изображений героев Штормграда...','','','','','','','','',''),
(14620,'Unpleasant place, this \"Undercity\". Not at all like the Lordaeron of old. How I miss it...$b$bIf you\'re looking to go to Stratholme, I\'m afraid I\'m unable to assist at the moment. The towers nearby the burning city are still in contention, and as such my powers are far too weak to aid you. Return to me once you\'re victorious there.','여기 언더시티란 곳은 정말 마음에 안 들어. 옛 로데론의 모습은 전혀 찾아볼 수가 없단 말일세. 아, 그 얼마나 그리운 이름인가...$b$b지금 스트라솔름으로 가볼 작정이라면 내 도움을 받을 생각은 꿈에도 하지 말게나. 그 불타오르는 도시 근처의 탑들은 아직 전쟁의 소용돌이에 휩싸여 있고 내 하찮은 능력은 자네에게 별 도움이 되지 않으니까 말이야. 자네 진영이 거기서 성공을 거두면, 날 다시 찾아오게.','C’est un endroit bien déplaisant, cette « Fossoyeuse ». Il ne ressemble pas du tout au Lordaeron des temps anciens. Comme il me manque…$b$bSi vous voulez vous rendre à Stratholme, j’ai bien peur d’être en ce moment dans l’incapacité de vous prêter assistance. Les tours qui se trouvent près de la ville incendiée sont toujours disputées, et mes pouvoirs sont trop faibles pour que je puisse vous aider. Revenez me voir quand vous aurez été $gvictorieux:victorieuse; là-bas.','Unangenehmer Ort, dieses \'Unterstadt\'. Ganz und gar nicht wie das alte Lordaeron. Wie ich es vermisse...$b$bWenn Ihr nach Stratholme wollt, kann ich Euch im Moment nicht helfen. Um die Türme nahe der brennenden Stadt wird noch gekämpft, deshalb reichen meine Kräfte nicht aus. Kommt wieder, wenn Ihr dort siegreich seid.','“幽暗城”这种煞风景的地方，怎比得上洛丹伦废墟。我真怀念那儿啊……$B$B你想去斯坦索姆？恐怕眼下我没法帮你。在那座燃烧的城市附近，哨塔争夺战仍在继续；而且我的力量太过薄弱，真是爱莫能助啊。如果你能成功夺得哨塔，再来找我吧。','這個「幽暗城」是個令人感到不愉快的地方。一點也不像舊時的羅德隆。我真是想念它...$b$b如果你正期待前往斯坦索姆，恐怕我現在無法幫你。燃燒城市附近的哨塔仍在爭奪中，而我的力量太過微弱以至於無法協助你。等你在那裡獲得勝利後再回來找我。','Un lugar horrendo, esta \"Entrañas\". Nada que ver con lo que era Lordaeron antes. Cómo extraño esa época... $b$bSi lo que quieres es ir a Stratholme, me temo que no te puedo ayudar ahora mismo. Las torres cercanas a la ciudad ardiente todavía están en disputa, por lo que mis poderes son leves como para echarte una mano. Regresa a mí una vez hayas conseguido una victoria allí.','Un lugar horrendo, esta \"Entrañas\". Nada que ver con lo que era Lordaeron antes. Cómo extraño esa época... $b$bSi lo que quieres es ir a Stratholme, me temo que no te puedo ayudar ahora mismo. Las torres cercanas a la ciudad ardiente todavía están en disputa, por lo que mis poderes son leves como para echarte una mano. Regresa a mí una vez hayas conseguido una victoria allí.','Пренеприятнейшее место – этот \"Подгород\". Совсем не похоже на старый Лордерон. Как же я по нему скучаю...$b$bЕсли вы ищете возможности попасть в Стратхольм, то, боюсь, сейчас я ничем не могу вам помочь. За башни близ горящего города по-прежнему идут бои, и силы мои слишком слабы, чтобы помочь вам. Возвращайтесь ко мне, когда одержите там победу.','','','','','','','','',''),
(14621,'Ah, I can sense it - you\'ve won the day! I believe I can safely transport you to Stratholme now, provided you\'ve paid my colleague there a visit first. Just step into the circle and be patient...','그래, 자네 진영이 승리했다는 사실이 느껴지는군! 이제 자네가 스트라솔름까지 안전하게 순간이동할 때가 되었네. 단, 자네가 내 동료를 먼저 만나봤다면 말이지. 자, 원형 안으로 들어와서 조용히 기다리게...','Ah, je le sens… Vous avez gagné ! Je pense que je vais pouvoir maintenant vous transporter jusqu’à Stratholme, si vous avez pris le soin auparavant de rendre une petite visite à mon collègue qui se trouve là-bas. Entrez simplement dans le cercle et attendez patiemment…','Ah, Ich kann es spüren - dies ist Euer Tag! Ich glaube, ich kann Euch jetzt sicher nach Stratholme transportieren, wenn Ihr meinem Kollegen dort bereits besucht habt. Tretet in den Kreis und habt etwas Geduld...','啊，我能感受到——你获胜啦！如果你已经拜访过我在斯坦索姆的同伴，我想现在我能将你安全传送到那儿了。来，走到法阵中来，耐心等待……','啊，我可以感覺到 - 你成功了!如果你已先拜訪了我那裡的同事，我相信現在可以安全地將你傳送至斯坦索姆了。踏進那個圓圈裡耐心等候...','Ah, puedo sentirlo... ¡Hoy es tu día! Creo que te puedo transportar a Stratholme, siempre que le hayas hecho una visita allí a mi compañero. Simplemente párate en medio del círculo y espera...','Ah, puedo sentirlo... ¡Hoy es tu día! Creo que te puedo transportar a Stratholme, siempre que le hayas hecho una visita allí a mi compañero. Simplemente párate en medio del círculo y espera...','А, я это чувствую! Ты $gпобедил:победила;! Думаю, я могу теперь безопасно доставить тебя в Стратхольм при условии, что ты первым навестишь моего коллегу. Становись в круг и жди...','','','','','','','','',''),
(14692,'It does my soul good to see the walls of Stormwind standing strong and tall.$b$bIf you\'re looking to go to Stratholme, I\'m afraid I\'m unable to assist at the moment. The towers nearby the burning city are still in contention, and as such my powers are far too weak to aid you. Return to me once you\'re victorious there.','스톰윈드를 둘러싼 높은 성벽이 당당한 위용을 자랑하는 모습을 보니 내 마음이 참으로 흡족하군.$b$b지금 스트라솔름으로 가볼 작정이라면 내 도움을 받을 생각은 꿈에도 하지 말게나. 그 불타오르는 도시 근처의 탑들은 아직 전쟁의 소용돌이에 휩싸여 있고 내 하찮은 능력은 자네에게 별 도움이 되지 않으니까 말이야. 자네 진영이 거기서 성공을 거두면, 날 다시 찾아오게.','Cela me fait chaud au cœur de voir que les murailles de Hurlevent restent hautes et puissantes.$b$bSi vous avez l’intention de vous rendre à Stratholme, j’ai bien peur d’être en ce moment dans l’incapacité de vous prêter assistance. Les tours qui se trouvent près de la ville incendiée sont toujours disputées, et mes pouvoirs sont trop faibles pour que je puisse vous aider. Revenez me voir quand vous aurez été $gvictorieux:victorieuse; là-bas.','Es tut gut, die Mauern von Sturmwind so stark und sicher zu sehen.$b$bWenn Ihr nach Stratholme wollt, kann ich Euch im Moment nicht helfen. Um die Türme nahe der brennenden Stadt wird noch gekämpft, deshalb reichen meine Kräfte nicht aus. Kommt wieder, wenn Ihr dort siegreich seid.','看着雄伟的暴风城城墙高耸、壁垒森严、固若金汤，真是令人倍感欣慰。$B$B你想去斯坦索姆？恐怕眼下我没法帮你。在那座燃烧的城市附近，哨塔争夺战仍在继续；而且我的力量太过薄弱，真是爱莫能助啊。如果你能成功夺得哨塔，再来找我吧。','這正是我所希望見到的暴風城壯碩、聳立的城牆。$b$b如果你正期待前往斯坦索姆，恐怕我現在無法幫你。燃燒城市附近的哨塔仍在爭奪中，而我的力量太過微弱以至於無法協助你。等你在那裡獲得勝利後再回來找我。','Me alegra ver una Ventormenta fuerte y pujante.$b$bSi lo que quieres es ir a Stratholme, me temo que ahora mismo no te puedo ayudar. Las torres en las cercanías de la ciudad ardiente todavía están en disputa, y por ello no tengo poder suficiente para ayudarte. Regresa a mí una vez hayas conseguido conquistarlas.','Me alegra ver una Ventormenta fuerte y pujante.$b$bSi lo que quieres es ir a Stratholme, me temo que ahora mismo no te puedo ayudar. Las torres en las cercanías de la ciudad ardiente todavía están en disputa, y por ello no tengo poder suficiente para ayudarte. Regresa a mí una vez hayas conseguido conquistarlas.','Душа моя радуется при виде крепких и высоких стен Штормграда.$b$bЕсли ты хочешь попасть в Стратхольм, боюсь, прямо сейчас я не смогу тебе помочь. Башни рядом с горящим городом все еще состязаются, и у меня слишком мало сил для помощи тебе. Одержи там победу – и возвращайся ко мне.','','','','','','','','',''),
(14693,'Ah, I can sense it - you\'ve won the day! I believe I can safely transport you to Stratholme now, provided you\'ve paid my colleague there a visit first. Just step into the circle and be patient...','그래, 자네 진영이 승리했다는 사실이 느껴지는군! 이제 자네가 스트라솔름까지 안전하게 순간이동할 때가 되었군. 단, 자네가 내 동료를 먼저 만나봤다면 말이지. 원형 안으로 들어와서 조용히 기다리게...','Ah, je le sens… Vous avez gagné ! Je pense que je vais pouvoir maintenant vous transporter jusqu’à Stratholme, si vous avez pris le soin auparavant de rendre une petite visite à mon collègue qui se trouve là-bas. Entrez simplement dans le cercle et attendez patiemment…','Ah, Ich kann es spüren - dies ist Euer Tag! Ich glaube, ich kann Euch jetzt sicher nach Stratholme transportieren, wenn Ihr meinem Kollegen dort bereits besucht habt. Tretet in den Kreis und habt etwas Geduld...','啊，我能感受到——你获胜啦！如果你已经拜访过我在斯坦索姆的同伴，我想现在我能将你安全传送到那儿了。来，走到法阵中来，耐心等待……','啊，我可以感覺到 - 你成功了!如果你已先拜訪了我那裡的同事，我相信現在可以安全地將你傳送至斯坦索姆了。踏進那個圓圈裡耐心等候...','Ah, puedo sentirlo... ¡Hoy es tu día! Creo que te puedo transportar a Stratholme, siempre que le hayas hecho una visita allí a mi compañero. Simplemente párate en medio del círculo y espera...','Ah, puedo sentirlo... ¡Hoy es tu día! Creo que te puedo transportar a Stratholme, siempre que le hayas hecho una visita allí a mi compañero. Simplemente párate en medio del círculo y espera...','Ах, я чувствую – вы одержали победу! Уверен, что могу без риска перенести вас в Стратхольм – с условием, что вы сначала нанесете визит моему коллеге. Встаньте на этот круг и потерпите немного...','','','','','','','','',''),
(14744,'Please cast a high priority DEBUFF spell on all nearby targets.','주위에 있는 모든 대상에게 상급 약화 마법을 시전하십시오.','Veuillez lancer un sortilège d\'AFFAIBLISSEMENT de haute priorité sur toutes les cibles à proximité.','Bitte wirkt einen Schwächungszauber mit hoher Priorität auf alle in der Nähe befindlichen Ziele.','请为附近所有的目标施放高级的减效法术。','請對附近所有目標施展高優先權的減益法術。','Lanza un hechizo de PERJUICIO de alta prioridad sobre todos los objetivos cercanos.','Lanza un hechizo de PERJUICIO de alta prioridad sobre todos los objetivos cercanos.','Пожалуйста, наложите приоритетный ОТРИЦАТЕЛЬНЫЙ эффект на все цели, которые находятся поблизости.','Please cast a high priority DEBUFF spell on all nearby targets.','주위에 있는 모든 대상에게 상급 약화 마법을 시전하십시오.','Veuillez lancer un sortilège d\'AFFAIBLISSEMENT de haute priorité sur toutes les cibles à proximité.','Bitte wirkt einen Schwächungszauber mit hoher Priorität auf alle in der Nähe befindlichen Ziele.','请为附近所有的目标施放高级的减效法术。','請對附近所有目標施展高優先權的減益法術。','Lanza un hechizo de PERJUICIO de alta prioridad sobre todos los objetivos cercanos.','Lanza un hechizo de PERJUICIO de alta prioridad sobre todos los objetivos cercanos.','Пожалуйста, наложите приоритетный ОТРИЦАТЕЛЬНЫЙ эффект на все цели, которые находятся поблизости.'),
(14745,'Please cast a high priority BUFF spell on all nearby targets.','주위에 있는 모든 대상에게 상급 강화 마법을 시전하십시오.','Veuillez lancer un sortilège d\'AMÉLIORATION de haute priorité sur toutes les cibles à proximité.','Bitte wirkt einen Stärkungszauber mit hoher Priorität auf alle in der Nähe befindlichen Ziele.','请为附近所有的目标施放高级的增益法术。','請對附近所有目標施展高優先權的增益法術。','Lanza un hechizo de VENTAJA de alta prioridad sobre todos los objetivos cercanos.','Lanza un hechizo de VENTAJA de alta prioridad sobre todos los objetivos cercanos.','Пожалуйста, наложите приоритетный ПОЛОЖИТЕЛЬНЫЙ эффект на все цели, которые находятся поблизости.','Please cast a high priority BUFF spell on all nearby targets.','주위에 있는 모든 대상에게 상급 강화 마법을 시전하십시오.','Veuillez lancer un sortilège d\'AMÉLIORATION de haute priorité sur toutes les cibles à proximité.','Bitte wirkt einen Stärkungszauber mit hoher Priorität auf alle in der Nähe befindlichen Ziele.','请为附近所有的目标施放高级的增益法术。','請對附近所有目標施展高優先權的增益法術。','Lanza un hechizo de VENTAJA de alta prioridad sobre todos los objetivos cercanos.','Lanza un hechizo de VENTAJA de alta prioridad sobre todos los objetivos cercanos.','Пожалуйста, наложите приоритетный ПОЛОЖИТЕЛЬНЫЙ эффект на все цели, которые находятся поблизости.'),
(14746,'The Northpass tower needs our aid! Once again, let us charge and do proud or liege!','북부관문 경비탑에 지원이 필요하다! 다시 한번 진군하여 우리 군주님을 기쁘게 해드리자!','La tour du Col du nord a besoin de notre aide ! Chargeons une fois encore, que notre suzerain soit fier de nous !','Der Nordpassturm braucht unsere Hilfe! Lasst uns noch einmal ruhmreich voranstürmen!','北地哨塔需要我们的支援！冲啊！','北地哨塔需要我們的協助!讓我們再一次衝鋒陷陣，展現傲氣和忠誠!','La Torre del Paso Norte necesita tu asistencia. Debemos controlarla y ser el orgullo de nuestra estirpe.','La Torre del Paso Norte necesita tu asistencia. Debemos controlarla y ser el orgullo de nuestra estirpe.','В башне Северного Перевала нужна наша помощь! Давайте же ринемся в бой и прославим господина!','','','','','','','','',''),
(100000,'This songflower plant stands out as a rock in the sea of corruption that is Felwood. Its petals have a powerful fragrance that bolsters your spirits and strengthens your resolve.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这种歌花植物就像费伍德森林腐败海洋中的一块岩石一样引人注目。 它的花瓣具有浓郁的香气，可以振奋您的精神并增强您的决心。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'This songflower plant stands out as a rock in the sea of corruption that is Felwood. Its petals have a powerful fragrance that bolsters your spirits and strengthens your resolve.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这种歌花植物就像费伍德森林腐败海洋中的一块岩石一样引人注目。 它的花瓣具有浓郁的香气，可以振奋您的精神并增强您的决心。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100001,'This windblossom plant stands out as a beacon of light in the darkness that is Felwood. Plump and juicy berries hang from the plant, ripe for the picking.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这种风花植物在费伍德森林的黑暗中脱颖而出，成为一盏灯塔。 饱满多汁的浆果挂在植物上，成熟后可供采摘。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'This windblossom plant stands out as a beacon of light in the darkness that is Felwood. Plump and juicy berries hang from the plant, ripe for the picking.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这种风花植物在费伍德森林的黑暗中脱颖而出，成为一盏灯塔。 饱满多汁的浆果挂在植物上，成熟后可供采摘。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100201,'Ah, if it isn\'t $N! You’ve certainly become famous around here.\n\nYou need to get to Goldshire? Well, I can\'t deny you after all you\'ve done for us. I will be able to teleport you there this one time as a special favor.\n\nAre you ready to go? It will be a while before you can return back here once you leave.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'啊，如果不是 $N 的话！ 你在这附近肯定已经出名了。\n\n你需要去闪金镇吗？ 好吧，在你为我们所做的一切之后，我不能拒绝你。 这次我可以把你传送到那里，作为一个特殊的恩惠。\n\n你准备好出发了吗？ 离开这里之后，需要一段时间才能回到这里。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100002,'This healthy whipper root plant stands as a polar opposite to the sickly taint of corruption that dominates Felwood. Tender and healthy roots yield delicious tubers that lay on the ground next to the plant.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这种健康的鞭根植物与费伍德森林中盛行的腐败腐败截然相反。 柔嫩健康的根部会长出美味的块茎，长在植物旁边的地上。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'This healthy whipper root plant stands as a polar opposite to the sickly taint of corruption that dominates Felwood. Tender and healthy roots yield delicious tubers that lay on the ground next to the plant.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这种健康的鞭根植物与费伍德森林中盛行的腐败腐败截然相反。 柔嫩健康的根部会长出美味的块茎，长在植物旁边的地上。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100200,'It\'s so good that you\'re here with me $N, what can I do for you?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你能和我在一起真是太好了$N，我能为你做什么吗？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100003,'This vibrant night dragon plant stands in stark contrast to the demonic taint that sunders Felwood. Rare and luscious fruit, known as Night Dragon\'s Breath, hang heavily from the plant.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这种生机勃勃的夜龙植物与撕裂费伍德森林的恶魔污染形成鲜明对比。 稀有而甘美的果实，被称为“夜龙之息”，沉重地挂在植物上。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'This vibrant night dragon plant stands in stark contrast to the demonic taint that sunders Felwood. Rare and luscious fruit, known as Night Dragon\'s Breath, hang heavily from the plant.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这种生机勃勃的夜龙植物与撕裂费伍德森林的恶魔污染形成鲜明对比。 稀有而甘美的果实，被称为“夜龙之息”，沉重地挂在植物上。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100004,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<Chromie looks at you with a pale face.>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<克罗米脸色苍白地看着你。>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100100,'As you inspect the plane more carefully, you notice the words \"Property of Nert Blastentom\" scribbled onto the side.\n\nThe plane is decorated with small stickers. Among them are a small coin, a yellow parrot, and a hammer.\n\nThe words \"FM Acquisition\" are inscribed onto the bottom.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'当你更仔细地检查飞机时，你会注意到飞机侧面潦草地写着“纳特·布拉斯滕托姆的财产”。\n\n飞机上装饰有小贴纸。 其中有一枚小硬币、一只黄鹦鹉和一把锤子。\n\n底部刻有“FM Acquisition”字样。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(16680,'I am Falstad, Thane of the Wildhammer Clan. Can you smell it upon the air, the foul stench of troll lingers like a taint upon The Hinterlands.\n\nThe trolls have been encroaching ever closer to Aerie Peak, and it is our job to stifle them at every chance that we can.\n\nSo, what are you doing here, what is it the Wildhammer can do for you?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我是法斯塔德，蛮锤氏族的领主。你能否闻到空气中的气味，巨魔的恶臭像瘴气一样萦绕在辛特兰上。\n\n巨魔已经越来越接近鹰巢峰，我们的工作就是抓住一切可能的机会来压制他们。\n\n那么，你在这里做什么，蛮锤能为你做什么？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(17907,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Unicorns are noble creatures.  Make sure to always treat yours well; there are fewer things more dangerous than an angry unicorn.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'独角兽是高贵的生物。 请确保始终善待你的独角兽；很少有什么比愤怒的独角兽更危险的了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(18925,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'You\'ll be purchasing no mount here until you\'ve proven your worth and dedication to our people.$b\nDo not return until you are considered exalted among the high elves. Away with you!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'在证明您的价值和对我们人民的奉献之前，您不能在这里购买任何坐骑。$b\n除非你被认为在高等精灵中是崇高的，否则不要再回来！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30001,'You know.. Nothing... I was more powerful then all of you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你知道…你什么都不知道…我曾比你们所有人都更加强大。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30002,'We embrace the darkness now... Come and be lettin\' me show you its power!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'现在我们拥抱黑暗……来吧，让我向你展示它的力量！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30003,'Hahahaha! I be the Hazzuri Champion, what you be mon?!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'哈哈哈哈！我是哈祖里的冠军，你是什么，朋友？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30004,'I rule over Zul\'Hazu... You shall never kill me...',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我统治着祖尔哈祖...你永远不能杀我...',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30005,'The Furbolg must survive! I will do anything to ensure it!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'熊怪必须存活下去！为了保证这一点，我愿意做任何事情！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30006,'The Grove must be protected! You won\'t stop me!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'必须保护小树林！ 你阻止不了我！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30007,'Your interference will not stop us!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你的干涉无法阻止我们！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30008,'I have served the Master faithfully! You shall not interfere!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我忠诚地为主人服务！你不能干扰！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30009,'You... You aren\'t supposed to be here, get away!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你……你不应该在这里，走开！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30010,'This is my domain, you are not allowed to be here!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这是我的领地，你不能在这里！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30011,'I can see through the veil... I was wrong... Thank you, brave one, I am free.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我能看透迷雾……我错了……谢谢你，勇者，我自由了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30012,'To be wise is to have knowledge, to heed the advice of those who have seen, and know more than yourself. If you wish to truly advance in this world, you must reach out into areas of discomfort, and of which you have no experience. Grow, and experience new things, and seek new knowledge. In time, you will gain wisdom in many things young one.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'要明智意味着拥有知识，听从那些比你更有见识、更了解事物的人的建议。如果你想在这个世界上真正取得进步，你必须涉足不熟悉的领域，去经历你没有经验的事物。成长，体验新事物，寻求新知识。随着时间的推移，你将在许多方面获得智慧，年轻人。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30013,'To be virtuous is to be a just, and good person, the villages of our kind were built on the actions of the good hearted. In your travels there will be many decisions to make, and always you must look out for the good outcome of all, and not just yourself. To make a sacrifice for the good of your kin is to live with virtue, remember this always and do what is right.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'要具有美德意味着成为一个公正和善良的人，我们这种人类的村庄是建立在善良之人的行动基础之上的。在你的旅途中，会有许多决定需要做，你必须始终考虑到所有人的利益，而不仅仅是自己。为了族人的利益而做出牺牲是具有美德的选择，永远记住这一点，并做正确的事情。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30014,'To live with humility is to live with modesty, to never take more than what is neccesary, and to save everything with care for the future. Free yourself from pride, and arrogance, for they only get in the way of true progress. Do for those that cannot, and give what excess you have, to those that may be in need, be a pillar of the community, there may come dark days, when people need someone to look up to for support, let it be you, young one.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'谦逊地生活意味着谨慎地生活，不要拿超出所需的东西，要小心保存一切，为将来做好准备。摆脱傲慢和自大，因为它们只会妨碍真正的进步。为那些无法做的事情努力，并将你多余的东西给予那些可能需要的人，成为社区的支柱。可能会有黑暗的日子，人们需要有人被仰望来支持，让这个人就是你，年轻人。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30015,'Oh boss mon, ya can\'t take da whole crew with ya, da rest got stuff of dey own to do and da ship be not ready to sail yet. Ya gonna have to do dis da hard way.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'哦，老板，你不能带走所有船员，其他人还有自己的事情要做，而且船还没准备好出航呢。你得自己硬着头皮来做这件事。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30016,'It seems death claimed me $r, I am Sovatir, Arcanist and Lorekeeper of Eldre\'thalas, I have placed a part of my soul and memories in that journal, when you spoke the incantation you brought it up. I should let you know that it ate at your life force however, not too much I trust.\n\nSince you\'re now the owner of the journal, you\'re also mine, my knowledge is yours as long as you keep me entertained and allow me to find even more. Do note, that nobody else can see me.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'起来死神已经宣告了我的离世，$r，我是索瓦提尔，埃尔德雷萨拉斯的奥术师和知识守护者。我将我的一部分灵魂和记忆放在了那本日志里，当你念出咒语时，你唤醒了它。不过我得提醒你，那可是会消耗你的生命力，不过并没有太多，我相信你会没事的。\n\n既然你现在是这本日志的主人，你也是我的主人，我的知识将与你分享，只要你让我感到有趣，并让我继续寻找更多的知识。请注意，其他人是看不到我的。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30017,'There seems to be something in this crate.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这个箱子里好像有什么东西。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30018,'The dock here? Well you could catch the ship that used to sail to that Night Elf place. What\'s it\'s name? Uhh Auberdine I think.\n\nAye. You better try Stormwind City Harbor. At least I heard people travel from Stormwind nowadays. I don\'t really know for sure, I just load and unload stuff.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这里的码头？ 好吧，你可以搭上那艘曾经航行到暗夜精灵地方的船。 它叫什么名字？ 呃，我想是奥伯丁。\n\n是啊。 你最好试试暴风城港口。 至少我听说现在人们都从暴风城出发旅行。 我不太确定，我只是负责装卸货物。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30019,'I took Cookie on the ship when he was very young, he was hostile and bitter at first but through that book, you\'ve found we had developed a bond. In a way Cookie was able to understand anyone without actually knowing a word they were saying.\n\nNot sure what to tell you matey, Cookie was my friend and I\'ve sent you to end him, which may be my greatest regret yet.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'当库奇还很小的时候，我就把他带上了船，一开始他充满敌意和怨恨，但通过那本书，你会发现我们已经建立了一种联系。 在某种程度上，库奇能够理解任何人，而无需真正知道他们在说什么。\n\n不知道该告诉你什么，伙计，库奇是我的朋友，我派你来结束他的生命，这可能是我迄今为止最大的遗憾。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30020,'I am infused with the power of the tiger, I will win, no matter how many new scars I gain along the way!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我融合了猛虎的力量，我会获胜的，无论我在这个过程中获得多少新的伤痕！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30021,'Take a look upon my wares. I am the best tailor in this lightforsaken town.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'看看我的货物吧。我是这个被圣光遗弃的小镇上最好的裁缝。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30022,'The times are tough, but there\'s always opportunity for business.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'时局艰难，但商机总是存在的。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30023,'I thought I would only be putting slacking miners in cages, now for a real fight!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我本以为我只是要把懒惰的矿工关进笼子里，现在却要迎接一场真正的战斗！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30024,'Dammit. I knew they would find me. Alas, all good things come to an end. Before we fight for our lifes, tell me who sent you. Was it Maltimor?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'该死。我知道他们会找到我。唉，所有美好的事情总会有终结的时候。在我们为生命而战之前，告诉我是谁派你来的。是马尔蒂莫吗？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30025,'Of course it was him, the old fool. He thinks that my death will fix everything... Oh, how wrong he is. My death will change nothing!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'当然是他这个老傻子了。 他认为我的死会解决一切……哦，他真是错得离谱。我的死什么都改变不了！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30026,'If only you knew... Maltimor, I hope the Twisting Nether... takes you...',NULL,NULL,NULL,'如果你知道的话……马尔蒂莫，我希望扭曲虚空……带走你……',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30027,'That was a bad deal...',NULL,NULL,NULL,'那是一笔糟糕的交易...',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30028,'We, Darkspear, had to flee our homeland twice. Once, when the Gurubashi drove us from Stranglethorn, and then the naga drove us away from the Isles. We know the feeling of loss.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我们，暗矛部族，不得不两次逃离我们的家园。首先，在古拉巴什驱逐我们离开荆棘谷，然后是纳迦将我们赶离了群岛。我们懂得失去的感觉。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30029,'I see it too. Yet I have trouble believing their intents. Among the few Troll tribes left in Kalimdor, the Sandfury had a terrible reputation, even before Ukorz took over.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我也看到了。 但我很难相信他们的意图。 在卡利姆多仅存的几个巨魔部落中，沙怒甚至在乌科兹接管之前就享有可怕的声誉。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30030,'The Horde welcomes anyone who does not fit anywhere else. Thrall welcomed the Darkspear in spite of Troll history with the Second Horde. I cannot leave them, my kind, in the desert.\n\nI be not saying they join the Horde yet, but we will help. And stop the madness in Zul\'Farrak.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'部落欢迎任何不适合其他地方的人。萨尔在考虑到巫毒部落与第二次部落的历史后欢迎了暗矛部族。我不能将他们，我的同类，留在沙漠中。\n\n我不是说他们现在就要加入部落，但我们会提供帮助。并且制止祖尔法拉克的疯狂。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30031,'I be Vol\'jin, son of Sen\'jin. It be a long time since we fled our lands of the Darkspear Isles, but here in Durotar we found a new home and future alongside the Horde.\n\nOur tribe be resilient, and no matter how the river flow, the stones remain. Stay away from the Voodoo, and may the Loa forever guida ya steps mon.\n\nFor the Darkspear and for the Horde!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我是沃金，森金的儿子。自从我们逃离暗矛岛的土地以来已经过了很长时间，在杜隆塔尔，我们在部落的陪伴下找到了新的家园和未来。\n\n我们部族坚韧不拔，无论河水如何流动，石头都不会变。远离巫毒，愿洛阿永远引领你的步伐，伙计。\n\n为了暗矛，为了部落！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30032,'There are many secrets in this swamp, it just takes a keen eye to search for it.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这片沼泽里隐藏着很多秘密，只需要一双敏锐的眼睛就能寻找到。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30033,'The murloc hut looks abandoned, and unkempt.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这个鱼人小屋看起来已经被遗弃了，荒废不堪。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30034,'The nest is empty.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这个巢穴是空的。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30035,'What? She told this to a stranger? Oh by the light, this is... this is worse than I thought. Please, speak to Marge Blackwood, she is the investigator in this town, and responsible for several cases currently. Speak to her, she will explain it all. Somehow I think I\'m sleeping outside tonight anyhow.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'什么？她竟然告诉一个陌生人这个？哦，天啊，这真的……比我想象的更糟糕。请和玛吉·布莱克伍德谈谈，她是这个镇上的侦探，目前负责几个案件。和她交谈，她会解释一切。不管怎样，我估计今晚我要露天睡了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30036,'Ahem, I\'ve been told to read this out to anyone inquiring further, some if it might make no sense, at least it doesn\'t to me, so here we go...\n\n\"The Art located here is created by players on the server, and is a community outlet to host more in the future, the museum may expand or grow depending on contributions made! We would like to thank each and every person who has contributed or submitted such fabulous artwork. ~ Turtle Staff\"\n\nSee, it doesn\'t make much sense to me either.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'咳咳，我被告知要把这篇文章读给任何进一步询问的人听，有些可能没有意义，至少对我来说没有意义，所以我们开始吧……\n\n这里展示的艺术作品是由服务器上的玩家创作的，这是社区提供的一个平台，将来可以容纳更多，博物馆可能会根据作品的贡献而扩大或发展！我们要感谢每一个为此贡献或提交了如此出色艺术作品的人。\n~ 海龟工作人员”\n你看，这对我来说也没有多大意义。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30037,'Northshire Abbey sure is a nice, and quiet place.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'北郡修道院确实是一个美好而安静的地方。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30038,'The enemy draws near brothers and sisters of the Horde! Answer the call for war, and fight off the enemies that dare challenge us!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'敌人已经临近，部落的兄弟姐妹们！响应战争的呼唤，击退那些胆敢挑战我们的敌人',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30039,'We Magram are stuck in a war with our enemies, we are known for our bravery, unlike the Gelkis who live in caves...\n\n I am Khan here, what can you do for me?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我们玛格兰人正陷入与敌人的战争中，我们以勇气闻名，不像居住在洞穴中的吉尔吉斯人…\n\n我是此地的可汗，你能为我做些什么？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30040,'<The Khan stares with wild eyes.>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<可汗用狂野的眼神盯着。>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30041,'You have spirit of Magram. Drink. Share of our blood. Become Magram. Become strong. Become us!\n\n<The towering Khan holds out a filled skull goblet filled with curdling red blood.>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你有玛格兰的精神。喝。分享我们的血。变成玛格兰。变得强大。变成我们！\n\n<高大的可汗伸出一个装满凝结红色鲜血的骷髅酒杯。>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30044,'I am Shaka, I rule here, I lead the Gelkis, do not think to be bold, outsider, it would be unwise.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我是沙卡，我统治着这里，我领导着吉尔吉斯部落，外来者，不要妄想傲慢，那是不明智的。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30045,'You have helped Gelkis more than any outsider before. We wish to offer you blessing, make you honorary Gelkis!\n\n<The towering Khan holds out a ritualistic bowl of powerful incense.>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你对吉尔吉斯的帮助比任何外人都多。 我们愿为您送上祝福，使你成为荣誉的吉尔基斯人！\n\n<高大的可汗伸出一只充满仪式感的碗，里面装着强大的香料。>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30046,'Wretched Horde scum! You shall be unended from this earth for all the treachery and misery you have brought to the world!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'可恶的部落败类！你们为世界带来了背叛和痛苦，你们将被从这个世界上消灭！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30047,'Kul Tiras will never forget the suffering you have brought to Azeroth... You shall never know peace.. as long as the anchor stands...',NULL,NULL,NULL,'库尔提拉斯永远不会忘记你给艾泽拉斯带来的苦难……你永远不会知道和平……只要矛还矗立着……',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30048,'What is it that you want pup?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你想要什么，小家伙？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30049,'You shall be cursed, for all eternity!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你将受到永恒的诅咒！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30050,'If only h-he , had loved me back...',NULL,NULL,NULL,'要是他、他也爱我就好了……',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30051,'An ancient gong that looks incredibly aged.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\n一架看起来非常古老的古代锣。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30052,'Everything! Ambushes, attacks, the wildlife itself rose up in rebellion, and even the damn MONKEYS came from the trees and attacked all my workers!\n\nWe had bases all along the island, with sustainable and PROFITABLE harvesting, and now it\'s all gone bananas because of some apes and the king named Morgo... or something.\n\nWe\'re short-staffed, undermanned and sorely in need of help, so quit asking questions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'一切都错了！伏击、袭击，甚至野生动植物也起来反抗了，那些该死的猴子从树上跳下来，攻击我的所有工人。\n\n我们在整个岛上建立了基地，进行可持续、有利可图的收获，但现在一切都变成了一团糟，都是因为一些猿猴和他们的国王名叫摩戈... 或者什么别的。\n\n我们人手不足，资源匮乏，急需帮助，所以别再问问题了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30053,'Tel\'Abim is looking for anyone to take up the following bounties, payment will be given upon proof of completion!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'特尔阿比姆正在寻找愿意接下以下赏金任务的人，完成任务后将支付报酬！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30054,'It\'s mine, I aint givin\' it back!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这是我的，我不会还回去！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30055,'The Cat Spirits gaze pierces through your soul.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'猫灵的目光能够穿透你的灵魂。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30056,'Yes, according to the legend, during this time of the year, the Ancient walks the land once more. Where exactly I cannot say. As previously stated, our interaction is usually through the dreams that our druids have.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'是的，根据传说，在每年的这个时候，远古之灵会再次走过大地。具体在哪里我无法说。正如之前所述，我们与它的互动通常是通过我们的德鲁伊在梦中进行的。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30057,'Hmm... The tales never speak where one can physically find the Winter Patriarch, but Mulgore has been our ancestral home for ages, and even when driven away, we find our way back there. I would begin my search there.Take care when searching for legends young one, you may find answers you never sought out to begin with.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'嗯... 传说从未透露过在哪里可以找到寒冬族长，但莫高雷是我们的祖传之地，即使被驱赶，我们也会找回自己的路。我会从那里开始寻找。当寻找传说时要小心，年轻人，你可能会找到你从未寻求的答案。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30058,'You seek Father Bear? Ah then Ashenvale is where you must go. It is said that Father Bear resides in the icy slopes of Mount Hyjal all year except for this time, the time of the year where he descends to Ashenvale. Be careful not to stoke his fury should you find him.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你在寻找熊爸爸吗？ 啊，那么灰谷就是你必须去的地方。 据说，熊爸爸一年四季都居住在海加尔山冰冷的山坡上，除了这个时候，他每年都会下到灰谷。 如果你找到他，请小心不要激怒他。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30059,'Ya be seeking \'im? Then ya need to search our land. Da Spirit was here long before da Dwarves, and will continue to be here long after they be dead.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你在找他吗？那么你需要在我们的土地上搜索。 大精灵早在矮人出现之前就已经存在了，并且在矮人死后很长一段时间内仍将继续存在。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30060,'Eh? Ye realize it\'s a legend? Regardless, ye wouldn\'t be the first to seek out a legend. It is said he walks the land at this time of the year blanketing it in snow. Dun Morogh is snowy year round, so I recommend searching the surrounding areas. Perhaps Loch Modan or the Wetlands? Search the mountains in between perhaps.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'嗯？你意识到这只是个传说吗？不管怎样，你不会是第一个寻找传说的人。据说他在每年的这个时候走遍大地，覆盖它们以雪。丹莫洛是一年四季都下雪，所以我建议在周围地区搜索。也许洛克莫丹或湿地？或许搜索中间的山脉吧。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30061,'Heh? Ya wanna sit on his lap or somethin\', yer in luck cause he\'s right here in the Vale! He won\'t allow you to sit on his lap though, but for a small fee you can get a painting made with him!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'嘿？你想坐在他的腿上还是什么，你运气不错，因为他就在谷地里！虽然他不允许你坐在他的腿上，但只需支付少量费用，你就可以得到一幅与他一起创作的画！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30062,'Well, where to begin? I traveled to Westfall and helped establish a church there. The locals were extremely friendly, religious folk themselves, and assisted in whatever manner they could. Me and them both brought the community together, created strong bonds and helped eachother when we were able.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'那么，从哪里开始呢？ 我前往西部荒野并帮助在那里建立了一座教堂。 当地人本身就非常友好、有宗教信仰，并尽其所能地提供帮助。 我和他们都将社区凝聚在一起，建立了牢固的联系，并在力所能及的情况下互相帮助。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30063,'There was trouble though, between two families, the Molsen and Easton, a land dispute of sorts that dated back a generation, marriage problems between them, who owned what, and which property belonged to who.\n\nThe Molsens got it in their head that they would inherit the Easton estate, especially a young one, went by the name Carver, a ruffian of a lad, who got himself into all sorts of trouble.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'然而，莫尔森和伊斯顿这两个家庭之间存在着一些麻烦，比如可以追溯到上一代人的土地纠纷，他们之间的婚姻问题，谁拥有什么，哪些财产属于谁。\n\n莫尔森一家的想法是，他们将继承伊斯顿的遗产，尤其是一个年轻的孩子，名叫卡佛，是一个问题少年，给自己惹上了各种各样的麻烦。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30064,'It was around this time that the thugs began to show up, the boy Carver was quick to join them. The Defias threatened families to leave their land with acts of violence and murder.\n\nSoon after the Easton family was murdered in cold blood, and many other families simply left, not wanting to face similar fates.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'就在这个时候，暴徒们开始出现，男孩卡弗很快也加入了他们的行列。 迪菲亚兄弟会以暴力和谋杀行为威胁家庭离开他们的土地。\n\n伊斯顿家族被冷血谋杀后不久，许多其他家庭就干脆离开了，因为他们不想面对类似的命运。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30065,'Less, and less showed up to my church, I had a small following, but the Defias made their presence known, threatened me to leave, and even beat me near death for refusing. I was stubborn, but not stubborn enough to die. So I left for Stormwind, where my tale continues now.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'人数越来越少来参加我的教堂，我有一小群追随者，但迪菲亚兄弟会的存在变得越来越明显，他们威胁我离开，甚至因为我拒绝而将我打得半死。我很顽固，但不至于固执到要死。所以我前往了暴风城，我的故事现在在那里继续。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30066,'I... I should explain. Yes, I was lying to you all this time. I made the golems, with the help of Farad and some goblin machinery. We had lived here, in Moonbrook, many years ago.\n\nWe just wanted to escape this shithole. So we made the Harvest Golems, to help the farmers and, also, to get their money. But we knew that it was too expensive for an average farmer to buy one. So we were selling them for a low, low price. We were losing a lot of money on it.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我...我应该解释一下。是的，我一直在欺骗你们。我和法拉德以及一些地精机器的帮助制造了这些魔像。多年前，我们就住在这里，月溪镇。\n\n我们只是想离开这个烂摊子。所以我们制造了收割魔像，帮助农民，还有，赚点他们的钱。但我们知道普通农民买一个太贵了。所以我们以很低的价格出售。我们在这上面亏了很多钱。\n\n\n\n\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30067,'You probably already know where it is going. I\'m not proud of this part. There was a catch. When everyone\'s fields were protected by golems, we would activate their true nature.\n\nThey would become murderous machines. We would blame it on some vile warlock, or anyone else, it didn\'t matter. Only important thing was that we would be the only ones who could fix them, for a very high price.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你可能已经猜到了接下来会发生什么。我对这部分并不自豪。有个条件。当每个人的田地都被魔像保护时，我们会启动它们的真正本性。\n\n它们会变成杀人的机器。我们会把它归咎于某个邪恶的术士，或者其他人，不重要。唯一重要的是，我们是唯一能够以非常高的价格修复它们的人。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30068,'At least, that was the idea. In my greed, I activated the murderous killswitch when Farad was working with some golems in a workshop. I wanted him to die, so all the money would go to me.\n\nI learned later that he survived, and only got blinded. He hated me for it. But regardless, I saw the destruction I caused. I wanted to make the golems docile again… but our spell didn\'t work.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'至少，那是最初的想法。出于我的贪婪，我在法拉德在车间里与一些魔像一起工作时启动了杀人的开关。我希望他死了，这样所有的钱就会进我的口袋。\n\n后来我得知他活下来了，只是失去了视力。他对我充满了仇恨。但无论如何，我看到了我造成的破坏。我想让魔像再次变得温顺……但是我们的法术没有起作用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30069,'Some mistake we made during construction, or just lack of skill, I will never know. I couldn\'t fix them. Westfall became a wasteland. And then, came the Defias, with Farad on their side.\n\nAnd you know the rest of this story. You may judge me, think of me as a monster. The truth is, that you are probably right. I was a monster. But I did everything I could to fix it. And by the Light, I can only hope that it is enough.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'在建造过程中我们犯了一些错误，或者只是技能不足，我永远不会知道。我不能修复它们。西部荒野变成了一片废墟。然后，达菲尔出现了，法拉德站在他们一边。\n\n你知道这个故事的其余部分。 你可能会评判我，认为我是一个怪物。 事实是，你可能是对的。 我是一个怪物。 但我已尽我所能来解决它。 以圣光之名，我只能希望这已经足够了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30070,'I\'m glad that you wish to assist us. I will do my best to recap where we stand.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我很高兴你愿意帮助我们。我会尽力回顾一下我们的现状。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30071,'I will explain the situation. I am Caledra Dawnbreeze, formerly a Ranger-Captain of the Farstriders during the Second War, but now merely a citizen of Stormwind. After the loss of Quel\'Thalas, our people suffered deeply due to our addiction to magic.\n\nSome of us, led by our former prince, Kael\'thas, were seduced by dark magic, and, from what I\'ve heard, they betrayed the Alliance by siding with the creatures known as the Naga.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我会解释一下情况。我是卡莱德拉·黎明之风，曾在第二次战争期间担任远行者的游侠队长，但现在只是暴风城的一名市民。在失去奎尔萨拉斯之后，我们的人民因为对魔法的沉迷而遭受了深重的打击。\n\n我们中的一些人，由我们的前王子凯尔萨斯领导，被黑暗魔法所诱惑，据我听说，他们背叛了联盟，与被称为纳迦的生物结盟。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30072,'I\'ve heard other... more troubling accounts, but regardless, they are lost to us. We should focus on those who have chosen to remain in the Alliance. A few months ago, I managed to gather representatives of our people from all outlying settlements such as the Farstrider lodges.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我听说过其他……更令人不安的说法，但无论如何，我们都失去了它们。 我们应该关注那些选择留在联盟的人。 几个月前，我设法从远行者小屋等所有边远定居点召集了我们人民的代表。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30073,'There was a meeting where it was agreed upon that the time has come for our people to join their efforts so that we may create a home for ourselves. One where we could rebuild our people in time. Living in a military lodge or cities belonging to other races simply isn\'t the way to make progress in reforming our culture.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'在一次会议上，我们一致认为，现在是我们的人民共同努力的时候了，这样我们就可以为自己创造一个家园。在那里，我们可以在未来重建我们的种族。 生活在军事小屋或属于其他种族的城市中根本不是在改革我们的文化方面取得进展的方法。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30074,'Thankfully Dalaran\'s surviving archives provided an opportunity. Roughly a century ago, an outpost was built on a peninsula near Quel\'Thalas. The outpost is powered by an arcane crystal infused with the energies of the Sunwell itself.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'值得庆幸的是，达拉然幸存的档案提供了一个机会。 大约一个世纪前，奎尔萨拉斯附近的一个半岛上建立了一个前哨基地。 该前哨站由注入了太阳之井本身能量的奥术水晶提供动力。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30075,'In other words, it\'s a way for us to cope with the addiction to magic that we\'ve been suffering from. The crystal will not last forever, but it will buy us time to find a cure.\n\nOur scouts have managed to find the site, and they\'ve confirmed that it is inhabitable. Our people have begun to settle the outpost, and they have named it Alah\'Thalas, the Land of Light in our tongue.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'换句话说，这是我们应对魔法成瘾的一种方法。 水晶不会永远存在，但它可以为我们赢得时间来寻找治疗方法。\n\n我们的侦察员已经成功找到了该地点，并且他们确认该地点适合居住。 我们的人民已经开始在这个前哨基地定居，他们将其命名为阿拉萨拉斯（Alah\'Thalas），我们语言中的光之地。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30076,'However, the buildings are old and have not been maintained properly. We lack the reagents and materials to sustain the enchantments that protect the outpost.\n\nLikewise, the local mine has been infested with creatures. In other words, any help you provide would be greatly appreciated!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'然而，这些建筑年代久远，没有得到妥善维护。 我们缺乏试剂和材料来维持保护前哨站的结界。\n\n同样，当地的矿井也充满了生物。 换句话说，我们将非常感谢您提供的任何帮助！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30077,'Alleana? Ah, I see. She should have visited in person! Of course I will help.$B$B Tell her that it is all about apperance and mannerisms: Speaking to the fledglings not as a parent, not as a master, but as a friend and an equal. They will respect this approach, and only by earning their respect can she hope to bridge the gap between them.$B$BRemember that they are still wild creatures. Their strength and service they lend to us by their own will, not because we tame them or demand it of them.$B$BPlease return to Allie with this advice, and if you could also tell her... I often still press my lips to her letters at night. She really should come visit me for private tutelage someday.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'阿莉安娜？ 啊，我明白了。 她应该亲自来看看！ 我当然会帮忙。$B$B 告诉她这一切都与外表和举止有关：与初出茅庐的孩子说话，不是作为父母，不是作为主人，而是作为朋友和平等的人。 他们会尊重这种做法，只有赢得他们的尊重，她才有希望弥合他们之间的差距。$B$B记住，他们仍然是野生生物。 他们按照自己的意愿向我们提供力量和服务，而不是因为我们驯服了他们或要求他们这样做。$B$B请将此建议返回给艾莉，如果你也能告诉她...晚上我经常还会亲吻她的信，她真的应该有一天私下来看望我，接受私人辅导。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30078,'Yes, Alleana did write to me with her concerns a few months back. Those Moonfeathers are blessed in that they have a natural talent for communion with Elune’s favored creatures, who look upon them with respect. $B$BHmm... If they do not acknowledge her or her words, perhaps she has not yet gained the respect of the forest. The fledglings will know if she is one of their chosen by instinct alone. It has been too long since I visited the forests of our birth, but I am certain there must be a forest king or patriarch who would judge her as worthy.$B$BPerhaps she should seek out one of these creatures and earn their favor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'是的，几个月前阿莉安娜确实写信给我表达了她的担忧。 这些月羽族人受到了祝福，因为它们拥有与艾露恩最喜爱的生物交流的天赋，而艾露恩的生物也对他们充满敬意。 $B$B嗯...如果他们不承认她或她的话，也许她还没有赢得森林的尊重。 雏龙们会知道她是否是他们凭本能选择的人之一。 我已经很久没有去过我们出生的森林了，但我确信一定有一位森林之王或族长会判断她是否配得上这份尊荣。$B$B也许她应该去找一个这样的生物，赢得它们的青睐。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30079,'Oh my word, how awful!$B$BAlleana is a Moonfeather, yes? I have every confidence she will find the method that works best for her. Every master handles the hippogryphs differently, as it is an intensely personal practice.$B$BThat said, I have heard the eastern reaches of our sacred forests are being ravaged much like the north. My condolences go out to her, and may Elune grant her strength. Perhaps taking a break to relax her mind would help.$B$BOne cannot hope to calm a wild beast while also being of an uncalm mind, after all.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'噢，我的天，太糟糕了！$B$B阿莉安娜是月羽族人，是吗？ 我完全相信她会找到最适合她的方法。 每个大师处理角鹰兽的方式都不同，因为这是一种非常个人化的做法。$B$B 也就是说，我听说我们神圣森林的东部地区正像北部一样遭到破坏。 我向她表示哀悼，并愿艾露恩赐予她力量。 也许休息一下放松心情会有所帮助。$B$B 毕竟，无法在内心不宁的情况下安抚一只野兽。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30080,'<He looks up from replenishing the food for his charges and wipes the sweat from his brow with mucky, worn hands.>$B$BI am extremely busy right now performing my duties, $c. If Alleana wishes to follow in her siblings\'\' footsteps, she had best be prepared to put in the hours, days, years of blood, sweat, and tears to earn such an austere position.$B$BYou will excuse me.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<他从补充食物的工作中抬起头来，用脏兮兮、疲惫不堪的双手擦去额头上的汗水。>$B$B我现在非常忙于履行我的职责，$c。 如果阿莉安娜希望追随她兄弟姐妹的脚步，她最好准备好投入数小时、数天、数年的血、汗和泪水，以获得如此严肃的职位。$B$B请原谅我。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30081,'Sharptalon tenses visibly as you approach, but relaxes at the mention of the Moonfeather name. Eventually, his wings stop beating, he nestles to the ground below, and bows his head, letting out a deferential trill.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'当你接近时，利爪明显紧张，但在提到月羽的名字时放松了下来。 最终，他的翅膀停止了拍打，依偎在下面的地面上，低下头，发出恭敬的啁啾声。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30082,'It\'s a matter of strategy and value of life. That\'s what this all comes down to. Starwind has rallied those who she commands, made their blood boil with speeches about glory and defending the homeland. Noble, but we are not some troll berserkers! We are Kaldorei, noble, strong, intelligent. It is with the greatest of pain in my chest I see apprentices and young sentinel sisters, some barely past their first century, racing off to skirmish with orcs and goblins in the felled trees of our homeland.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这是策略和生命价值的问题。这就是问题的实质。 星风已经召集了她指挥的人，通过关于荣耀和保卫家园的演讲让他们热血沸腾。这是高尚的，但我们不是巨魔狂战士！ 我们是卡多雷，高贵、强大、聪明。 当我看到学徒和年轻的哨兵姐妹时，我的胸口感到无比痛苦，其中一些才刚过一百岁，冲向我们家园倒下的树木中，与兽人和地精进行小规模的冲突。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30083,'Of course we could help them. We could charge into the fray with the others, into a maelstrom of steel and claws, blood and rage. We could grab the horde where they are strongest, and use our brute strength to expel them. But to think I would give the call, to be responsible for loss of life when it is so preventable? Then you are as foolish as her.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我们当然可以帮助他们。 我们可以与其他人一起冲入战斗，冲入钢铁与利爪、鲜血与愤怒的漩涡中。 我们可以在部落最强大的地方出击，利用我们的蛮力将他们驱逐出去。 但是，要让我下达这个指令，要为生命的损失负责，，生命损失是可以避免的吗？ 那你就和她一样傻了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30084,'No! There are weaknesses we can exploit, key parts of the horde war machine we can destroy, leaving them helpless. We can win this war with minimal danger. As I mentioned, the hawk does not stand in front of the fox and fight on its terms...',NULL,NULL,NULL,'不！ 我们可以利用一些弱点，我们可以摧毁部落战争机器的关键部分，让他们陷入无助。 我们可以以最小的危险赢得这场战争。 正如我所提到的，鹰不会站在狐狸面前并按照狐狸的条件战斗......',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30085,'Precisely. It may seem cold and calculated to think of it like that, but I am not the one who sent young sisters into a pointless battle. My conscience is clear; this will be the quickest and most effective way of winning. Trust me, even if that brash commander does not!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'正是如此。 这样想可能会显得冷酷和算计，但我不是那个让年轻姐妹陷入无意义战斗的人。 我的良心是清白的； 这将是最快、最有效的获胜方式。 相信我，即使那个鲁莽的指挥官不这样做！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30086,'Of course, speak to Commander Starwind if you haven\'t already. But know this - every hour that goes by, another chosen of Elune will be laying clover-clad.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'当然，如果你还没有和星风指挥官交谈的话，请与她谈一谈。但请注意，每过去一个小时，另一个伊露恩的选民就会倒下。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30087,'The moment our scouts reported the incursions into our land, I rallied those stationed nearby. Indecision has led to the Horde developing outposts and building lumber mills!$B$BNo more, we say. Most of us have already gone to fight, but Ironglade speaks about hatching some master plan, of deception and whatever. Well, while he talks from the comfort of his chair, we are busy fighting. And the coward refuses to help, he wishes us to retreat and regroup!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'在我们的侦察员报告入侵我们领土的情况时，我立刻召集了附近驻扎的部队。犹豫不决导致部落在我们的领土建立了前哨站和伐木厂！$B$B我不再容忍，我们说。我们中的大多数人已经投身战斗，但铁林之剑谈论着一些大计划，关于欺骗和其他的。然而，当他从他舒适的椅子上说话时，我们正在忙于战斗。而那个懦夫拒绝提供帮助，他希望我们撤退和重新集结！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30088,'$c, you don\'t know much about our way of fighting, do you? We can blend into the shadows under the canopy of the trees, strike when we need to strike.$B$BThere is strength in this: a retreating sister will be aided by unseen arrows and knives. If we all retreat, the blood lost so far will be for nought, and many of us will be killed and captured in the process. Absolutely not.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'$c，你对我们的战斗方式了解不多，是吗？我们可以在树冠的阴影下融入到暗处，在需要时发动突袭。$B$B这其中有力量：撤退的姐妹将会受到看不见的箭和刀的支援。如果我们全部撤退，到目前为止流失的鲜血将毫无意义，而且在这个过程中会有很多人被杀害和俘虏。绝对不行。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30089,'We haven\'t got a choice. I will not show the Horde our backs, or have to explain away the cowardice of retreat, nor will I allow them a chance to capture us as we flee. Lend me your strength, if he will not. Let us break the back of the Horde and show them what it means to trespass into Kaldorei land.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我们别无选择。我不会让部落看到我们的落寞的背影，也不会为撤退的胆怯辩解，更不会让他们有机会在我们逃跑时俘虏我们。如果他不愿意，就把你的力量借给我。让我们击败部落，向他们展示侵犯卡多雷土地的后果。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30090,'Glory is a consequence, we sacrifice for our homeland. And I would much rather make those greenskins die for our homeland than us. Are you in agreement, or do you wish to tarry and delay like the others, while we are actually struggling?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'荣耀是结果，我们为家园牺牲。 我宁愿让那些绿皮为我们的家园而死，而不是我们。你同意吗，还是你想像其他人一样拖延和延迟，而我们实际上正在苦苦挣扎？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30091,'Feel free, but hurry. Talk to Brolthan IronGlade. Come back when you are ready to fight, with or without him.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'随意，但要快点。 与布罗森·铁林对话。 当你准备好战斗时回来，无论有没有他。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30092,'Thou may be pondering upon how I, Lord Ebonlocke, came to be in such a wretched condition. But like many tales of woe, mine started with an insatiable thirst for power. As the ruler of the Great Hamlet, I yearned for more, craving proximity to the seat of power in Stormwind, desiring to meet the most influential individuals, and striving to climb the ranks of society, ultimately aiming for the crown itself.$B$BIn my hunger for greater power, I was heedless of my own people, resorting to ruthless, brutal, and unjust deeds to get what I wanted. The atrocities I have committed are beyond what I can bear to recollect. Nevertheless, my misdeeds pale in comparison to the sins of Medivh, that accursed sorcerer whose wicked deeds continue to haunt me even in death.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你可能正在思考我，埃伯洛克大人，是如何陷入如此悲惨的境地的。 但就像许多悲惨的故事一样，我的故事始于对权力的永不满足的渴望。 作为大哈姆雷特的统治者，我渴望更多，渴望接近暴风城的权力宝座，渴望见到最有影响力的人物，并努力攀登社会阶层，最终目标是王冠本身。$B$B在我对更大权力的渴望中，我不顾自己的人民，诉诸无情、残酷和不公正的行为来得到我想要的东西。 我所犯下的暴行已经超出我所能承受的范围。 然而，与麦迪文的罪恶相比，我的罪行就显得苍白无力了，麦迪文是那个可恶的巫师，他的恶行甚至在我死后仍然困扰着我。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30093,'Many years have passed since I first set my sights on this towering structure, yearning to gain an audience with the great lord of Karazhan, Medivh. Oh, how I coveted his power and knowledge.$B$BThe secrets that lay hidden within Karazhan called out to me, promising dark magic and enigmatic mysteries that I could wield to further my goals. And so, I became obsessed, visiting the tower time and time again, forsaking my duties, my people, and even my own family, all for the chance to speak with the sorcerer.$B$BBut alas, my efforts were for naught, for Medivh never granted me an audience, no matter how fervently I beseeched him. I could see the lavish banquets and grand parties he hosted, to which others were invited. Why did he elude me so?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'自从我第一次看到这座高耸的建筑，渴望觐见卡拉赞伟大的领主麦迪文以来，已经过去了许多年。 哦，我多么渴望他的力量和知识。$B$B卡拉赞中隐藏的秘密向我呼唤，承诺着我可以运用黑暗魔法和神秘的奥秘来达成我的目标。 于是，我开始着迷，一次又一次地拜访这座塔，放弃了我的职责、我的人民，甚至我自己的家人，一切都是为了有机会与那位巫师交谈。$B$B但可惜的是，我的努力是徒劳的， 因为麦迪文从来没有接待过我，不管我多么热切地恳求他。 我可以看到他举办奢华的宴会和盛大的聚会，并邀请其他人参加。 他为何如此躲避我？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30094,'Now, with the benefit of hindsight, I realize the foolishness of my obsession. How much I had sacrificed for the fleeting promise of power, all for naught. And yet, my heart still aches with the regret of missed opportunities and wasted years. If only I had known then what I know now. But alas, the past is set in stone, and I am left to ponder the might-have-beens and the what-ifs, forever trapped in the shadow of my own obsession.$B$BThe day that changed everything arrived in the form of a simple raven. It flew into my abode, bearing a letter from none other than Moroes, the castellan of Karazhan, inviting me to a grand ball to be held within the tower\'s walls.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'现在，事后看来，我意识到我的痴迷是愚蠢的。 为了转瞬即逝的权力承诺，付出了多少牺牲，但一切都毫无意义。 然而，我的心仍然因错过机会和浪费岁月而感到遗憾。 要是我当时就知道我现在所知道的就好了。 但可惜的是，过去已成定局，我只能思考可能发生的事情和假设，永远陷入自己痴迷的阴影中。$B$B改变一切的那一天以 一只简单的乌鸦形式到来。 它飞进了我的住所，带着一封来自卡拉赞城主莫罗斯的信，邀请我参加在塔墙内举行的盛大舞会。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30095,'It was an opportunity I couldn\'t pass up, for it was my chance to finally meet the great Medivh and learn from his boundless wisdom.$B$BWithout a second thought, I rushed out of my castle and set off for Karazhan, leaving my duties and my people behind. I was driven by a feverish energy, a feeling that I simply had to be there, no matter the cost. Looking back now, I can\'t help but think that Medivh had already begun manipulating me, even before I had set foot within his hallowed halls.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这是一个我不能错过的机会，因为这是我终于见到伟大的麦迪文并学习他无边智慧的机会。$B$B没有再多想，我冲出了我的城堡，出发前往卡拉赞，离开 我的职责和我身后的人民。 我被一种狂热的能量所驱使，一种感觉我必须在那里，无论付出什么代价。 现在回想起来，我不禁想到，甚至在我踏入麦迪文神圣的殿堂之前，麦迪文就已经开始操纵我了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30096,'Upon reaching the tower, I was ushered inside and allowed to roam freely while Medivh himself mingled with the other guests. It was an experience I shall never forget, for the tower was alive with magic and wonder, the likes of which I had never seen before. Was this all just a game to Medivh? A way to toy with his guests, drawing them ever deeper into his web of influence and power?$B$BLooking back on that night, I realize that it was the beginning of the end for me. The first step on a path that would lead to my downfall, my ruin, and my eventual damnation.$B$BAs I wandered the twisting halls and endless ballrooms of Karazhan, time seemed to slip away from me. It felt as though mere moments had passed. It was then that I realized something was amiss, for the tower was now vastly different from the one I had been admiring just moments before.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'到达塔楼后，我被带进去并可以自由漫步，而麦迪文本人则与其他客人混在一起。 这是一次我永远不会忘记的经历，因为这座塔充满了魔法和奇迹，这是我以前从未见过的。 这对麦迪文来说只是一场游戏吗？ 一种玩弄他的客人的方式，让他们更深地陷入他的影响力和权力之网？$B$B回顾那天晚上，我意识到这对我来说是终结的开始。 这条道路上的第一步将导致我的垮台、毁灭和最终的诅咒。$B$BA当我漫步在卡拉赞扭曲的走廊和无尽的舞厅时，时间似乎从我身边溜走了。 感觉好像只过去了片刻。 就在那时，我意识到有些不对劲，因为现在的这座塔与我刚才欣赏的塔有很大不同。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30097,'Where once there had been merriment and laughter, now there was only emptiness and decay. Apparitions crawled through the corridors, their moans and whispers echoing through the empty halls. How much time had passed since I had first arrived? I could not say, for time flowed differently within the confines of Karazhan.$B$BIt was then that I looked upon my own body, only to find that there was no body to look upon. I, and all of the guests have been killed, our essences drained to fuel Medivh\'s dark plans. The realization hit me like a bolt of lightning, and I knew then that I had been a fool to ever trust in his power and seek his knowledge.$B$BThe memory of my own arrogance and obsession with power burned within me, a constant reminder of my own folly. And so I remain, a ghost of the past, forever cursed to haunt the halls of Karazhan and warn others of the dangers that lurk within.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'曾经有欢乐和笑声的地方，现在只剩下空虚和腐朽。 幽灵在走廊里爬行，他们的呻吟声和低语声在空荡荡的大厅里回响。 距离我第一次到达已经过去了多少时间？ 我无法说，因为在卡拉赞的范围内，时间的流动是不同的。$B$B就在那时，我看着自己的身体，却发现没有身体可以看。 我和所有客人都被杀了，我们的精髓被耗尽，为麦迪文的黑暗计划提供了动力。 这个认识像一道闪电一样击中了我，然后我就知道我一直是个傻瓜，竟然相信他的力量并寻求他的知识。$B$B我自己的傲慢和对权力的痴迷的记忆在我内心燃烧，一种持续不断的感觉 提醒我自己的愚蠢行为。 所以我仍然是一个过去的幽灵，永远被诅咒在卡拉赞的大厅中出没，并警告其他人潜伏在其中的危险。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30098,'Bound to this cursed tower, my spirit lingers, tormented by the memories of my past and the horrors that surround me. The darkness of this place has consumed the souls of those who once walked these halls, leaving them lost and deranged. Yet, I have managed to hold onto my sanity, though barely.$B$BI do not seek revenge against Medivh, for I have long since accepted my fate. Instead, my only desire is to uncover the secrets that he kept hidden in this tower. As a ruler, I sought power and knowledge, and now, I am driven by that same hunger, but for different reasons.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我的灵魂被束缚在这座被诅咒的塔楼上，徘徊不去，被过去的记忆和周围的恐怖所折磨。 这个地方的黑暗吞噬了那些曾经走过这些大厅的人的灵魂，让他们迷失和疯狂。 然而，我还是勉强保持了理智。$B$B我不会向麦迪文报仇，因为我早已接受了自己的命运。 相反，我唯一的愿望是揭开他隐藏在这座塔中的秘密。 作为统治者，我寻求权力和知识，现在，我被同样的渴望所驱使，但出于不同的原因。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30099,'The Lower Part of Karazhan holds only a fraction of the knowledge that I seek. The true power of this tower can only be accessed through the Upper Part, which is sealed off by Moroes, the castellan. He guards the key to the Upper Tower with a fierce dedication and I believe that he serves an even darker master now…$B$BI implore you to help me uncover the mysteries of this tower. Share with me the knowledge that you find in the Upper Part of Karazhan. Together, we can piece together the truth of what happened in this cursed place and perhaps find some measure of peace for the tormented souls that still reside here.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'卡拉赞的下半部分只拥有我所寻求的知识的一小部分。 这座塔的真正力量只能通过被城主莫罗斯封锁的上部才能获得。 他以强烈的奉献精神守护着上塔的钥匙，我相信他现在侍奉着一个更加黑暗的主人……$B$B我恳求你帮助我揭开这座塔的神秘面纱。 与我分享你在卡拉赞上部发现的知识。 我们可以齐心协力，拼凑出这个被诅咒的地方所发生事件的真相，或许还能为仍然居住在这里的受折磨的灵魂找到某种程度的安宁。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30100,'Many believe that I retired after the destruction of Dalaran because I was old and tired of life. But the truth is, I left to hide in this remote place to avoid answering questions from those seeking the power hidden in Karazhan. I knew that someday, someone would come looking for me, seeking my knowledge to unlock the secrets of its chambers.$B$BI could simply turn you away with the key and keep my knowledge to myself, but deep down, I know that I cannot do that. I fear that darker powers than you can imagine have already taken up residence in the upper chambers of Karazhan, and time is running out to prevent them from being unleashed upon Azeroth.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'许多人认为我在达拉然毁灭后退休了，因为我年迈而且对生活感到厌倦。 但事实是，我躲在这个偏僻的地方是为了避免回答那些寻求卡拉赞隐藏力量的人的问题。 我知道有一天，有人会来找我，寻求我的知识来解开密室的秘密。$B$B我可以简单地用钥匙把你拒之门外，并将我的知识保密，但在内心深处，我知道我 不可以这样做。 我担心比你想象的更黑暗的力量已经在卡拉赞的上层房间中安家落户，而阻止它们向艾泽拉斯释放的时间已经不多了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30101,'The exact nature of powers that seek to harness the ley lines of Karazhan is still unknown to me, but in my dreams, I see a Burning Shadow slowly consuming all that I hold dear, and I cannot let this vision become a reality. I will not fail this time, not when the stakes are so high.$B$BI have failed in the past, and my failure nearly caused the destruction of the world. I allowed my friend, Medivh, to succumb to the darkness, and I cannot bear to make the same mistake again. Although I cannot change the past, I can help you avoid repeating it in the future. So, heed my warning and be prepared for the worst.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'那些试图驾驭卡拉赞魔网的力量的确切本质对我来说仍然是未知的，但在我的梦中，我看到燃烧之影正在慢慢吞噬我所珍视的一切，我不能让这个愿景成为现实。 这次我不会失败，赌注如此之高。$B$B我过去曾失败过，我的失败几乎导致了世界的毁灭。 我让我的朋友麦迪文屈服于黑暗，我无法忍受再犯同样的错误。 虽然我无法改变过去，但我可以帮助你避免将来重蹈覆辙。 因此，请注意我的警告并做好最坏的打算。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30102,'The land you see today used to be called the Kingdom of Corthan. For generations, every man that deserved the title of Marauder King was named Corthan, as the name of the land that he was to rule and serve for the rest of his life.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'那些试图驾驭卡拉赞魔网的力量的确切本质对我来说仍然是未知的，但在我的梦中，我看到燃烧之影正在慢慢吞噬我所珍视的一切，我不能让这个愿景成为现实。 这次我不会失败，赌注如此之高。$B$B我过去曾失败过，我的失败几乎导致了世界的毁灭。 我让我的朋友麦迪文屈服于黑暗，我无法忍受再犯同样的错误。 虽然我无法改变过去，但我可以帮助你避免将来重蹈覆辙。 因此，请听从我的警告并做好最坏的打算。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30103,'For many generations we had exactly what we wanted, we were a kingdom of war and of battle! Our thirst for combat was like no other. We were men of conquest and yet we never expanded our territory. Every defeated enemy knew its place.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'许多代人以来，我们都拥有我们想要的一切，我们是一个充满战争和战斗的王国！ 我们对战斗的渴望是无与伦比的。 我们是征服者，但我们从未扩张过我们的领土。 每个被击败的敌人都知道自己的位置。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30104,'As Keeper of the Living Flame for generations our sons and daughters were named either Zeth or Zetharia and they were meant to be the very image of our religion. You\'ve probably noticed that when we first spoke I said the curse of Zetharia. Indeed, it was my daughter that cursed us all into an eternity of undeath.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'作为“生命之焰”的守护者，我们的儿子和女儿被命名为赛斯或赛斯莉亚，他们本来就是我们宗教的形象。 你可能已经注意到，当我们第一次说话时，我说的是赛斯莉亚的诅咒。 事实上，是我的女儿诅咒我们所有人进入永恒的不死状态。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30105,'It is quite a long story. Zetharia had always loved Corthan, she knew nothing better on this world of ours, as our ancestors, the Azotha had left us on it, for better or worse. Her love of Corthan made her go mad.$B$BI had convinced the King that a union between him and the daughter of the Keeper would greatly help the kingdom and yet on the day of their marriage, Corthan showed up with his commoner mistress.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这是一个很长的故事。 赛斯莉亚一直爱着科森，她对我们这个世界一无所知，因为我们的祖先阿佐萨把我们留在了这个世界上，无论是好是坏。 她对科森的爱让她发疯了。$B$B我说服了国王，他和守护者的女儿之间的结合将极大地帮助王国，然而在他们结婚的那天，科森带着他的平民情妇出现了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30106,'I truthfully bear no ill mind to our king, friend. We do not choose those we love. But Zetharia, she had not taken well to this betrayal, as she called it.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'老实说，我对我们的国王并无恶意，朋友。 我们不选择我们所爱的人。 但赛斯莉亚并没有很好地接受她所说的这种背叛。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30107,'A dreadful pact Zetharia had committed, with the Lord of the Everlasting Death, and so she had cursed Corthan, his wife, and his kingdom to eternal undeath for the rest of time... Now, here we remain, lost to drift through time.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'赛斯莉亚与永恒死亡之主签订了一个可怕的契约，因此她诅咒了科森、他的妻子和他的王国，使其在余下的时间里永远不死……现在，我们留在这里，迷失在时间的流逝中。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30108,'What are you talking about? Don\'t make me call the guards!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你在说什么？ 别逼我叫警卫！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30109,'I didn\'t expect Livia to send a member of the Horde. What was she thinking?$B$BWhatever. Make sure this sealed report gets to her.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'没想到莉薇娅竟然派出了部落的成员。 她在想什么？$B$B无论如何。 确保她收到这份密封报告。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30110,'Even in the cold such as this, one can embrace the warmth found within the Light. Do you have a moment to pray $c?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'即使在这样的寒冷中，人们也可以拥抱圣光中的温暖。 你有时间祈祷吗？$c',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30111,'I have nothing to say to you. Begone from my sight.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我没有什么要对你说的。离开我的视线。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30112,'I do not believe we should associate. I cordially ask you to refrain from speaking to me again.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我不认为我们应该有任何交往。我诚恳地请求你不要再与我交谈。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30113,'The large valve hisses steam with intensity.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'那个大阀门发出强烈的蒸汽嘶嘶声。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30114,'An old lever with the following letters etched at the base$B$B\'Reserve Pump Lever.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'一个旧杠杆，底部刻有以下字母$B$B\'备用泵杆。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30115,'<The fire glows ominously.>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<火焰发出不祥的光芒。>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30116,'This mailbox appears to have been here for some time.$B$BAn aura of dread seems to emanate from it, you should not linger long.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这个邮箱似乎已经在这里有一段时间了。$B$B里面似乎散发着恐惧的气息，你不应该久留。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30117,'Are you familiar with what the Emerald Dream is, mortal?$B$BIn essence, Azeroth and the Emerald Dream can be perceived as parallel reflections of each other, intricately intertwined yet distinct in their nature. The Emerald Dream acts as a mystical lens, offering a pristine vision of Azeroth untouched by mortal intervention.$B$BWithin the Emerald Dream lies the original landmass of Kalimdor, unmarred by the cataclysmic Shattering, covered in lush, emerald-green forests that have flourished for aeons.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'凡人，你熟悉翡翠梦境是什么吗？$B$B本质上，艾泽拉斯和翡翠梦境可以被视为彼此的平行映像，错综复杂地交织在一起，但本质上却截然不同。 翡翠梦境就像一个神秘的镜头，提供了艾泽拉斯未被凡人干预的原始景象。$B$B翡翠梦境中坐落着卡利姆多的原始陆地，没有受到灾变性的破碎的破坏，覆盖着郁郁葱葱的翠绿森林， 繁盛万世。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30118,'Visitors from the waking world of Azeroth, both sentient and wild, unknowingly or knowingly, find themselves wandering into this ethereal domain.$B$BThese creatures enter the Dream through their slumber, bringing with them the whispers of the mortal realm. In this enchanted realm, dreams take on a profound significance, often weaving visions of prophecy and guidance for those who dare to listen.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'来自艾泽拉斯清醒世界的访客，无论是有感知的还是狂野的，无意或有意地发现自己漫游到这个虚幻的领域。$B$B这些生物通过睡眠进入梦境，带来了凡间的低语。在这个魔幻的领域里，梦想具有深远的意义，通常编织出预言和引导的愿景，为那些敢于倾听的人指引方向。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30119,'The Emerald Dream stands as the dominion of Ysera, the venerable Green Aspect, and we, the green Dragonflight, stand steadfastly by her side, resolute in our duty to protect this realm at all costs.$B$BThe majority of our kin dwell within the Dream, their spirits and physical forms intertwined within its ethereal embrace. Ages ago, guided by her infinite wisdom, Ysera selected one of our own, Solnius, to fulfill the pivotal role of the Awakener.$B$BBestowed with the power to rouse the green dragons from their slumber within the Dream in the face of dire perils, Solnius held a position of great responsibility.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'翡翠梦境是尊贵的绿龙之母伊瑟拉的领域，而我们，绿龙军团，坚定地站在她身旁，坚决履行我们不惜一切代价保护这个领域的职责。$B$B我们大部分的同胞都栖息在梦境之中，他们的灵魂和肉体在其空灵的怀抱中交织在一起。在很久以前，在她无尽的智慧的引导下，伊瑟拉选择了我们其中的一位，索尔纽斯，来履行觉醒者这一关键角色。$B$B被赋予了在面临严重危险时唤醒绿龙从梦境中的沉睡的力量，索尔纽斯承担了巨大的责任。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30120,'However, none among us could have foreseen the insidious emergence of the Nightmare. The Nightmare, a malevolent force of unknown origin, engulfs everything it touches, leaving naught but ruin and madness in its wake.$B$BAlas, Solnius has succumbed to the clutches of this vile corruption, his very essence ensnared within the grasp of the Nightmare.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'然而，我们谁都没有预见到梦魇的阴险出现。 梦魇，一种来历不明的邪恶力量，吞噬了它所触及的一切，只留下毁灭和疯狂。$B$B 可惜，索尔尼乌斯已经屈服于这种邪恶腐败的魔爪，他的本质陷入了梦魇的掌控之中。 恶梦。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30121,'We must prevent Solnius from awakening our kin from the Dream. Should their physical forms return to the mortal realm while fragments of their souls remain tethered to the Dream, they shall become profoundly susceptible to the insidious corruption of the Nightmare.$B$BThe corruption shall permeate their souls, eventually corrupting their physical forms, and the Nightmare shall find its pernicious path into Azeroth—a force that knows no bounds and defies all attempts to halt its advance.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我们必须阻止索尔尼乌斯将我们的同胞从梦境中唤醒。 如果他们的身体形态返回凡人领域，而他们的灵魂碎片仍然束缚在梦境中，他们将变得非常容易受到噩梦的阴险腐败的影响。$B$B 腐败将渗透到他们的灵魂，最终腐蚀他们的身体形态， 梦魇将找到它进入艾泽拉斯的凶险之路——一股无边无际的力量，无视一切阻止其前进的尝试。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30122,'Our only hope lies in the daunting task of halting Solnius and restoring him to the embrace of the Dream, even if it means resorting to the ultimate act of ending his life. It is our only hope.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我们唯一的希望就是阻止索尔纽斯，将他带回梦境的怀抱，即使这意味着不得不采取最终的行动，结束他的生命。这是我们唯一的希望。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30123,'I\'ll try to keep things short.$B$BGenn Greymane sought to shield Gilneas from the troubles that plagued the rest of the world. He firmly believed that we possessed the strength and resilience to stand alone, that the outside world brought nothing but strife. And for a time, it seemed he was right. Soon after the completion of the formidable Greymane Wall, the dread Scourge descended upon the North, leaving only desolation and ruins in its wake.$B$BYet, our isolated existence brought forth its own challenges. Scarce food and crippling trade restrictions plagued us. Scourge and worgen managed to find its way to our kingdom. Despite these hardships, the king remained steadfast, stubbornly refusing to open our gates and growing increasingly detached from his nobles and subjects.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我会尽量长话短说。$B$B吉恩·格雷迈恩试图保护吉尔尼斯免受困扰世界其他地区的麻烦。 他坚信，我们拥有独立的力量和韧性，外部世界只会带来冲突。 有一段时间，他似乎是对的。 令人畏惧的格雷迈恩之墙建成后不久，可怕的天灾降临到北方，留下的只是荒凉和废墟。$B$B然而，我们孤立的存在也带来了自己的挑战。 食物短缺和严重的贸易限制困扰着我们。 天灾军团和狼人设法进入了我们的王国。 尽管经历了这些困难，国王仍然坚定不移，顽固地拒绝打开我们的城门，并且与他的贵族和臣民越来越疏远。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30124,'He grew increasingly isolated, ensconced within the confines of his own family. And then came the Harlows, Alteraci scum who had found refuge within our walls. Whispering poison into Genn\'s ears, they further isolated him from his loyal nobles and common folk.$B$BTo preserve what scarce resources remained, many nobles, including myself, had our lands and possessions seized for redistribution. It was a painful blow, for I had been a vocal opponent of the king\'s decision. Stripped of my holdings, I was left with nothing but the fire of righteous indignation burning within me.$B$BThroughout this turmoil, Genn\'s unwavering love for his wife, Mia, provided a semblance of sanity. At her behest, he emerged from seclusion, organizing a public event to distribute food and clothing to the Gilnean populace. Regrettably, the meager resources quickly dwindled, leading to a confrontation between the common folk and the guards. In the ensuing chaos, Mia tragically lost her life.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'他变得越来越孤立，固守在自己的家族内部。 然后是哈洛斯家族，他们是奥特拉奇的败类，他们在我们的围墙内找到了庇护所。 他们在吉恩耳边低语毒言，进一步将他与忠诚的贵族和普通民众隔离开来。$B$B为了保护剩下的稀缺资源，包括我在内的许多贵族都被没收了我们的土地和财产进行重新分配。 这是一个痛苦的打击，因为我一直公开反对国王的决定。 我的财产被剥夺了，除了我内心燃烧的义愤之火之外，我一无所有。$B$B在这场动荡中，吉恩对妻子米娅坚定不移的爱，让我看起来很理智。 在她的要求下，他摆脱了隐居，组织了一场公共活动，向吉尔尼斯民众分发食物和衣服。 遗憾的是，微薄的资源很快就减少了，导致了平民和卫兵之间的对抗。 在随后的混乱中，米娅不幸丧生。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30125,'Devastated, Genn withdrew to the confines of his mansion, retreating from public view. The Harlow family seized power as regents, ushering in a reign of tyranny over Gilneas. Falsely accused of Mia\'s murder, I had no choice but to rally the support of the commonfolk and rise up against the oppressive regime.$B$BIn my heart, I know Genn is no longer among the living. Even in his compromised state, he would never have allowed such injustices to prevail. As we forge ahead in this rebellion, we strive to restore justice and bring about the liberation of Gilneas from the clutches of tyranny.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'吉恩悲痛欲绝，躲进了自己的宅邸，淡出了公众的视线。 哈洛家族作为摄政王夺取了权力，开启了对吉尔尼斯的暴政统治。 被诬陷谋杀了米娅，我别无选择，只能集结民众的支持，起来反抗专制政权。$B$B在我心里，我知道吉恩已经不在人世了。 即使在他妥协的状态下，他也绝不会允许这种不公正的事情发生。 当我们在这场叛乱中奋勇前进时，我们努力恢复正义，并将吉尔尼斯从暴政的魔掌中解放出来。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30126,'A hastily constructed grave. The following words are etched into the wood in crude handwriting.$B$B<Franklin Blackheart. Rest easy brother.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'一座仓促建造的坟墓。 以下文字以粗糙的笔迹刻在木头上。$B$B<富兰克林·黑心。 兄弟安息吧。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30127,'The stone hums softly.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'石头轻轻地嗡鸣着。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30128,'What have you done to Catherine? Stay back!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你对凯瑟琳做了什么？ 退后！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(40049,'I only sell my wares to the best of the champions, you think the spectators like you enough?\n\nIf so, step up, if not, back off pal!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我只向最出色的冠军出售我的商品，你认为观众喜欢你到什么程度？\n\n如果是这样，请上前一步；如果不是，请离开，伙计！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41028,'I bet you never expected to find fresh meat and drinks in the middle of this inhospitable swamp. You can hardly be blamed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我敢打赌，你绝不会预料到在这片荒凉的沼泽中会找到新鲜的食材和饮料。你几乎无法受到责备。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I bet you never expected to find fresh meat and drinks in the middle of this inhospitable swamp. You can hardly be blamed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I bet you never expected to find fresh meat and drinks in the middle of this inhospitable swamp. You can hardly be blamed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41083,'Best deals in Dun Agrath my friend, won\'t find any better. Now, what can I help you with?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我的朋友，顿格拉斯  最优惠的价格，找不到更好的了。 现在，我能为您提供什么帮助？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41084,'The Wildpaw Alpha notices the blood of the mighty and feared Korrak dripping off of you and cowers in submission.\r\n\r\nIt appears you have become the new alpha of this camp.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'狂爪阿尔法注意到强大而令人恐惧的科拉克的鲜血从你身上滴落，并畏缩屈服。\n\n看来你已经成为这个阵营的新阿尔法了。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41085,'<growl>\r\n\r\nThis gnoll does not appear intelligent enough to understand you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<低吼>\n\n这个豺狼人看起来不够聪明，无法理解你。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41333,'I don\'t have much time for idle talk, $N.  I\'ve got to get this bridge rebuilt before the rains come.  I\'ve finished every project on-time and under budget and I\'m not about to start slipping now.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我没有时间闲聊，$N。在雨季来临之前，我必须重新建造这座桥。我以往的每个项目都按时完成，还在预算内，现在也不会开始拖延。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41334,'Yes. A caravan with men and women dressed in scarlet passed through here. Many of our young ones followed them.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'是的。 一支商队，载着身穿猩红色衣服的男女，从这里经过。 我们的许多年轻人都跟随了他们。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41335,'I am really busy crafting this armor, so make it quick!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我正在忙着制作这套盔甲，所以请快点！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41336,'Aye, our young ones left with them. Can you blame them? Look at this place.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'是的，我们的孩子和他们一起离开了。 你能责怪他们吗？ 看看这个地方。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41337,'Who is this $c who goes before the Court of Lakshire in the Kingdom of Stormwind?  State your business within this township, $R.  The orc threat to the Kingdom is far too great to squander time in idle conversation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'这个在暴风王国拉克希尔宫廷受审的 $c 是谁？ 在这个城镇内陈述你的事务，$R。 兽人对王国的威胁太大了，不能把时间浪费在闲聊上。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41338,'It\'s regrettable that our children left with those foolish zealots of the crusade in the middle of the night! Please, don\'t harm them. Send them back home to us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'令人遗憾的是，我们的孩子在半夜和那些愚蠢的十字军狂热分子一起离开了！ 请不要伤害他们。 把他们送回家。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41339,'Before you lies the dead body of a Dwarf Mountaineer.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'你面前是一个死去的矮人山地探险家的尸体。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41343,'Greetings, potential customer! I\'ve got many rare herbs for sale. Take a look.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'您好，潜在的客户！ 我有很多稀有草药出售。 看一看。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(41344,'Yea boss, I sure did. I\'m a merchant, you know. If I got it, I sell it.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'是的，老板，我确实做到了。 我是个商人，你知道的。 如果我得到它，我就把它卖掉。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
