(100500,'Looking for a place to rest, $c?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'寻找休息的地方，$c？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Looking for a place to rest, $c?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'寻找休息的地方，$c？',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(195007,'The warrior who kills without showing his face has no honor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'杀人不露面的战士是没有荣誉的。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1000000,'It seems Mistress Abbendis was rash when choosing the new blood, if you were to have faced me at the entrance you wouldn\'t have made it this far.$B\nLook at you, monster, abomination. The way you move, the way you fight, the way you speak it\'s all driven by the strings of your Dark Master. If there\'s any morality left in you, pray to what you once knew as a powerful being.$B\nI have wasted breath on you, despicable creature, come and meet your end!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'看来阿比迪斯大人在选择新血的时候太草率了，如果你在入口处面对我的话你就不会走到这一步了。$B\n看看你，怪物，可憎的。 你的行动方式，你的战斗方式，你说话的方式，这一切都由你的黑暗大师的控制。 如果你还剩下一点道德，就向你曾经认为是强大的存在祈祷。$B\n我已经在你身上浪费了口气，卑鄙的生物，来见你的下场吧！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1000001,'For years, I have studied the arcane. My role in the order was different, yet meaningful. I have seen the work of necromancers in my studies. Never would I have imagined standing against such a powerful abomination as yourself.$B\nI believe it to be mockery-the fact you stand before me and have yet to attack. Do you, who carry the shame of your dark master, overestimate yourself this much? Alas, I will give you the satisfaction you seek.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'多年来，我一直在研究奥术。 我在订单中的角色不同，但很有意义。 我在学习中见过死灵法师的作品。 我从来没想过要对抗像你这样强大的可憎之物。$B\n我认为这是一种嘲讽——你站在我面前却还没有攻击。 背负着黑暗主子的耻辱的你，竟然这么高估自己了吗？ 唉，我会给你你想要的满足。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1000002,'I like to remember the Monastery as it used to be.$B\nA place of worship and joy, a place where the young would come in search of greater purpose. Sparring within these very halls, there were many I\'ve taught them how to defend themselves and what they stood for.$B\nMany were taken by the Light, butchered, and maimed by this unreasonable world. Nothing but toys to creatures like you that lavish in the pain and sorrow of righteous good people. I curse you, all of you. You believe us so weak to be defeated by a handful of wretched minions of the Scourge?$B\nCount your steps, they will be your last. When we are done with you, our shipwrights will be ready and we will find justice by our own means.$B\nYour downfall comes fools, I will protect the order!$B\nFor the Scarlet Crusade!',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我喜欢记住修道院以前的样子。$B\n一个崇拜和欢乐的地方，一个年轻人寻求更大目标的地方。 在这些大厅里，有很多人是我教他们如何保护自己以及他们所代表的东西的。$B\n许多人被圣光带走，被这个不合理的世界屠杀、残害。 对于像你这样的人来说，什么都不是，这些人在正义的好人的痛苦和悲伤中挥霍无度。 我诅咒你们，你们所有人。 你相信我们如此弱小以至于会被天灾军团的一小撮可怜的爪牙打败吗？$B\n数数你的脚步，这将是你的最后一步。 当我们处理完你之后，我们的造船工人就会准备好，我们会用我们自己的方式伸张正义。$B\n你的垮台来了，傻瓜，我会保护秩序！$B\n为了血色十字军！',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1000050,'We are about to witness a miracle of the Light. Alexandros Mograine is soon to be in our presence.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我们即将见证圣光的奇迹。 亚历山德罗斯·莫格莱尼很快就会出现在我们面前。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1000051,'I cannot rest. Not until I see the Scarlet Crusade fall and not until my son faces justice for killing his father.$B\nBut do not worry, someone else is to fulfill that task. Even in my rage, I would wish to hold my children in my arms for the last time. I am ready to rest on the other side, $N.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'我无法休息。 直到我看到血色十字军失败，直到我的儿子因杀害他的父亲而面临正义。$B\n不过不用担心，会有其他人来完成这个任务。 即使在愤怒中，我也希望最后一次将我的孩子抱在怀里。 我准备在另一边休息了，$N。',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
